  ('ea5d307a-4c0b-2445-b1e3-8f42f00d052b'::uuid, '3a419fce-ac79-274a-3319-c2c083fd26fa'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why run fast paper Crazy-8 sketching sprints before styling detailed screens in digital tools?', '', '["Software limits colors","Rapid sketching forces exploring contrasting concepts past obvious first clichés before pixel attachment forms","Clients prefer hand-drawn apps"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Fast divergent sketching dramatically broadens solution quality upfront.'),
  ('c3bf0875-1f2b-5698-aaab-d518c629ae13'::uuid, '3a419fce-ac79-274a-3319-c2c083fd26fa'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Which four UI states should accompany every major dynamic data screen?', '', '["Bold, Italic, Rounded, Flat","Ideal Populated, Helpful Empty, Loading Skeleton, and Error/Recovery","Desktop, Laptop, Monitor, TV"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Handling edge states cleanly prevents stranded blank dead ends in live use.'),
  ('7da5f93d-7788-8306-d1a8-8769a93063c1'::uuid, '3a419fce-ac79-274a-3319-c2c083fd26fa'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why does placing outer card separation smaller than inner element padding confuse screen scanners?', '', '["Triggers Javascript errors","Violates Gestalt Proximity, causing captions and actions to look grouped with neighboring cards","Reduces font weight"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Spatial grouping cues govern visual belonging effortlessly.'),
  ('42d7ef85-121e-0e47-f7c1-51dcbf155ef0'::uuid, '3a419fce-ac79-274a-3319-c2c083fd26fa'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'When running an unbiased usability test, what should a facilitator avoid doing?', '', '["Remaining politely silent during brief pauses","Prompting users with exact UI button names or guiding their mouse manually","Testing 5 target users"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Leading hints invalidate whether unassisted real users can navigate cleanly.'),
  ('21c57512-32b5-e031-d422-d975c8beaae7'::uuid, 'fb4ec98d-98b7-e83b-71ac-fc253db82c30'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why must form labels remain permanently visible rather than hiding strictly inside disappearing placeholder attributes?', '', '["Users forget field context once typing starts and screen readers/autofill handle persistent labels vastly better","Placeholders break CSS Grid","Browsers ban grey text"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Persistent labels plus 4.5:1 contrast keep forms inclusive and clear.'),
  ('3aaf0d11-2ee9-1b96-736a-127afc99fd38'::uuid, 'fb4ec98d-98b7-e83b-71ac-fc253db82c30'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'What prevents visual drift and "wrong hex grey" bugs between designers and frontend engineers?', '', '["Exporting flat JPEG screenshots","Synchronizing semantic Design Tokens (colors, 8px spacing scale, radii) paired with quick staging walkthroughs","Adding heavy drop shadows"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Shared token vocabulary aligns Figma/design specs cleanly with CSS code.'),
  ('acc3633a-a2a1-9394-09ca-11ebab8490bd'::uuid, 'fb4ec98d-98b7-e83b-71ac-fc253db82c30'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why should complex dense procedural text be converted into structured step or swimlane diagrams?', '', '["Diagrams reduce server bandwidth","Visual flow encoding clarifies order, ownership, and branches inside seconds without working-memory strain","Diagrams replace accessibility"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Spatial mapping surfaces conditional structure dramatically faster than prose walls.'),
  ('ad8c0ed7-2e31-7cfd-e9cb-dba130802e81'::uuid, 'fb4ec98d-98b7-e83b-71ac-fc253db82c30'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Which usability finding carries Severity 1 Blocker urgency prior to engineering ship?', '', '["Slight gradient adjustment on footer","Testers repeatedly fail submitting a checkout form because an overlapping floating icon hides Submit on mobile","Using 16px body text"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'High-frequency task failure blocks revenue and demands immediate pre-launch repair.'),
  ('0d910864-ce7e-649a-66e8-46a3b7d9cbf0'::uuid, 'fb4ec98d-98b7-e83b-71ac-fc253db82c30'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Why do senior reviewers prefer problem-led UI/UX case studies displaying early tested pivots over glossy galleries?', '', '["Demonstrates real research insight, constraint trade-offs, and user-verified design judgment cleanly","Glossy frames take longer to download","Portfolios require sketches legally"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explaining WHY iterations evolved proves true product-design capability cleanly.'),
  ('75935bfb-0eba-520b-c713-3de9f951d598'::uuid, 'bddead1a-9d01-d8cc-cc78-50fd9cecde64'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why test every brand logo concept strictly in 1-color monochrome at small 24px size before adding color?', '', '["Monochrome prints slower","Exposes silhouette clarity and scalability across favicons, stamps, and mobile icons cleanly without decorative color crutches","Clients dislike color"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Structural legibility must survive monochrome and tiny dimensions first cleanly.'),
  ('e71d145c-5466-52ab-bfb7-42113ffc3037'::uuid, 'bddead1a-9d01-d8cc-cc78-50fd9cecde64'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'What protects shared Canva templates from breaking when team members paste slightly longer headlines?', '', '["Using 8pt fonts","Anchoring headline frames cleanly into open whitespace buffers and locking logos/backgrounds","Converting text into photos"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Defensive frame anchoring keeps layouts neat across varied real copy lengths.'),
  ('491a11a9-abdb-ea14-cdc3-f9997ac82a52'::uuid, 'bddead1a-9d01-d8cc-cc78-50fd9cecde64'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'How should campaign photography be composed when intended to carry headlines and ad CTAs?', '', '["Center busy patterns everywhere","Frame subjects leaving clean uncluttered negative space (or subtle gradient scrim) safeguarding >= 4.5:1 text contrast","Use small yellow comic fonts"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Copy-safe framing preserves natural imagery while guaranteeing fast legibility.'),
  ('8905402e-a970-ac4b-d896-3622eaa7321e'::uuid, 'bddead1a-9d01-d8cc-cc78-50fd9cecde64'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why separate CMYK vector folders strictly from RGB digital exports inside final brand deliverables?', '', '["Prevents teams from accidentally placing low-res screen screenshots onto physical print runs or bloated print PDFs online","RGB forbids transparency","Canva blocks ZIP folders"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Clear destination folders prevent costly commercial print and web blunders cleanly.'),
  ('0f0d392e-659e-a699-cd92-6140f120cb32'::uuid, 'a23d3668-0cdd-0b4f-e908-fedae56d073e'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What belongs inside an actionable Brand Guideline Contrast Matrix table?', '', '["Poetic metaphors only","Explicit foreground/background hex pairs passing WCAG AA contrast alongside forbidden low-contrast pairings","Server IP logs"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Clear verified pairings eliminate illegible pastel-on-white social errors immediately.'),
  ('75654fe1-40af-76bc-0b4f-c41cedd98695'::uuid, 'a23d3668-0cdd-0b4f-e908-fedae56d073e'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'What distinguishes effective Art Direction across a multi-asset brand campaign?', '', '["Using 10 completely unrelated stock photo styles","Consistent lighting warmth, authentic subject framing, color grading, and shared surface mood across photos and layouts","Zero margins"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Cohesive sensory direction ties ads, web heroes, and print cleanly together.'),
  ('e919e449-167c-ddda-647c-4f4eeb173b6a'::uuid, 'a23d3668-0cdd-0b4f-e908-fedae56d073e'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why frame brand identity presentations around agreed positioning goals and realistic contextual mockups?', '', '["Helps stakeholders evaluate fit objectively against audience clarity rather than arbitrary personal color whims","Hides typography sizes","Avoids client questions"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Strategy-grounded mockups align decisions around real-world customer perception cleanly.'),
  ('6e47ac59-e8b2-abf4-47b4-38489975acbb'::uuid, 'a23d3668-0cdd-0b4f-e908-fedae56d073e'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'How do responsive Brand Identity systems stay legible from 16px favicons up to wide storefront banners?', '', '["Using one fixed cramped emblem everywhere","Providing a coordinated Logo Suite (Primary Horizontal, Stacked Vertical, simplified Icon Submark)","Stretching horizontal logos vertically"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Tailored logo variants preserve legibility across drastically different aspect ratios cleanly.'),
  ('98c1f387-e272-cdaf-484a-01e3a2aa7f07'::uuid, 'a23d3668-0cdd-0b4f-e908-fedae56d073e'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'What practical habit protects Instagram 4:5 (`1080x1350`) Canva carousel covers cleanly?', '', '["Placing vital title lines strictly within the center `1080x1080` safe zone so 1:1 profile grids never clip headlines","Typing edge-to-edge along corners","Using neon green strokes"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Center-safe design protects titles simultaneously in full feeds and cropped profile grids.'),
  ('4a7ec1e5-da56-3076-6ac5-5927f69e96c7'::uuid, '10251040-952f-7dc3-48f8-606dba7fbe24'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why does moving a subject beside a soft 45-degree window and checking viewfinder edges outperform harsh overhead indoor bulbs?', '', '["Windows add HDR metadata","Soft directional light shapes natural facial depth cleanly while edge scanning eliminates distracting messy backgrounds","Cameras forbid flash"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Light direction and background cleanup yield immediate editorial quality cleanly.'),
  ('26099b0a-03ff-c961-f8f6-9f593bc950e9'::uuid, '10251040-952f-7dc3-48f8-606dba7fbe24'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'When cutting dialogue inside video timelines, what ratio should background music generally sit relative to clear speech?', '', '["Equal 0 dB loudness","Ducked subtly `-24 to -30 dB` underneath clear `-6 dB` speech peaks so music supports without competing","Muted completely everywhere"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Background scores should frame emotion gently without ever forcing listeners to strain for words.'),
  ('c81839c7-f23a-5c7b-121b-3a239bcd764d'::uuid, '10251040-952f-7dc3-48f8-606dba7fbe24'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What replaces stiff robotic linear animation motion on entering titles and callouts?', '', '["Spinning 720 degrees fast","Smooth Ease-Out velocity curves settling gently into rest inside ~0.3–0.4s","12-second fades"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Natural physical deceleration feels crisp, refined, and effortless cleanly.'),
  ('45da6d3a-6c7d-2fac-e16b-aa53bf19798f'::uuid, '10251040-952f-7dc3-48f8-606dba7fbe24'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why export web and social photographs strictly under `sRGB` color profile sized cleanly to realistic display pixels?', '', '["Prevents washed-out browser color shifts while cutting bloated multi-megabyte load delays dramatically","sRGB converts PNG to SVG","Browsers ignore JPEG height"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Consistent `sRGB` color space plus tight pixel sizing delivers fast vibrant web imagery cleanly.'),
  ('a4d070e5-fe25-701f-b424-9fcd85ac6454'::uuid, 'ca1c9de8-7b01-7546-f53f-cff51e20f53a'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why assemble a video timeline’s spoken narrative ("Radio Cut") before scattering pretty B-roll clips across it?', '', '["Saves disk space","Verifies logical story arc and tight conversational rhythm purely through sound first before visual polish begins","Removes audio tracks"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Sound carries structural flow; strong Radio Cuts make visual B-roll elevation effortless cleanly.'),
  ('c76e8c3a-9feb-36d1-7795-64c2a21a037f'::uuid, 'ca1c9de8-7b01-7546-f53f-cff51e20f53a'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'How do J-cuts and L-cuts prevent abrupt jarring jumps between shots?', '', '["By compressing video bitrates","Overlapping incoming or outgoing audio slightly across visual edit points mirrors natural eye-ear transitions smoothly","Adding neon wipe stickers"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Split-audio overlaps create seamless editorial flow cleanly.'),
  ('60bd02d3-4793-3fc0-ecc0-f19bcad4f9b3'::uuid, 'ca1c9de8-7b01-7546-f53f-cff51e20f53a'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why must Color Correction (exposure + neutral white balance) precede creative LUT Color Grading?', '', '["LUTs disable timelines","Creative looks amplify uneven exposure and mismatched room bulbs into muddy erratic clips if footage isn’t neutralized first","Correction turns raw video into 60fps"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Balanced neutral footing lets subtle artistic grades harmonize seamlessly across cameras.'),
  ('cb362d5f-b4a6-bb85-2e4c-eb0f3f589ebc'::uuid, 'ca1c9de8-7b01-7546-f53f-cff51e20f53a'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What guarantees social vertical `9:16` burned-in captions remain completely readable on phones?', '', '["Placing text at the very bottom pixel edge","Proofreading AI transcripts for typos + keeping captions strictly inside center UI safe zones away from app overlays","Flashing random font colors"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Center safe margins plus human transcript checks protect clarity everywhere.'),
  ('b1a92529-82f9-d8fb-729f-ee3e5b2b0793'::uuid, 'ca1c9de8-7b01-7546-f53f-cff51e20f53a'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Why vary shot scale systematically (Tight Detail Hands -> Medium Face -> Wide Setting -> POV) when filming short documentaries?', '', '["Eliminates awkward jump cuts between identical medium angles and edits effortlessly into smooth visual rhythm","Uses less battery","Doubles file bitrate"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Planned shot variety solves editing headaches long before entering post-production cleanly.'),
  ('303086cb-f90a-e106-e051-e2cfebe9cdbf'::uuid, 'd23c0f7e-b68a-81b6-e01a-9879e13d2968'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Which HTML element provides native keyboard activation and focus semantics for UI actions?', '', '["<div class=\"btn\">","<button type=\"button\">","<span role=\"text\">"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Native <button> supports Tab focus, Enter/Space activation, and assistive roles out of the box.'),
  ('81ebde83-1fb5-7c3a-5682-70481e627ae5'::uuid, 'd23c0f7e-b68a-81b6-e01a-9879e13d2968'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why should form fields avoid relying solely on placeholder attributes without <label>?', '', '["Browsers disable autofill","Placeholders vanish while typing and leave users and screen readers without clear context","Labels add CSS grid tracks"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit visible labels preserve usability during editing and assistive navigation.'),
  ('92e1e571-3dea-e34b-32f0-722ea578a141'::uuid, 'd23c0f7e-b68a-81b6-e01a-9879e13d2968'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Which CSS rule creates an auto-flowing responsive grid without horizontal overflow?', '', '["width: 1200px fixed","grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr))","float: left on every child"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'auto-fit + minmax lets Grid adjust column counts fluidly to container width.'),
  ('05c629de-acbe-0cd9-e7ff-f8d5e9d03038'::uuid, 'd23c0f7e-b68a-81b6-e01a-9879e13d2968'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What defines an atomic Git commit?', '', '["All weekly edits in one commit","One self-contained logical change that builds and passes tests cleanly","Committing broken WIP hourly to main"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Atomic commits keep reviews sharp and allow isolated rollbacks.'),
  ('cb507c39-327c-93be-0469-bc38e3e4151f'::uuid, 'd23c0f7e-b68a-81b6-e01a-9879e13d2968'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'How do you prevent DOM XSS when rendering user-supplied text inside HTML templates?', '', '["Wrap text in <b> tags","Escape HTML entities or assign via textContent and validate URL schemes","Run eval() on input"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Proper escaping/textContent plus http/https URL checks prevent script injection.'),
  ('393a0f99-1880-34d2-077f-a1fbef97c1c4'::uuid, '1ae9367d-03f1-bec6-d004-742aa7467bb9'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'After resolving a Git merge conflict manually, what is the essential next step before pushing?', '', '["Force-push immediately","Re-run build/lint and automated tests to verify merged behavior","Delete package-lock.json"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Manual conflict resolution can easily break syntax or behavior if untested.'),
  ('bbf5d220-710e-dd05-c829-ed0ac242d9ef'::uuid, '1ae9367d-03f1-bec6-d004-742aa7467bb9'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why is event delegation preferred over binding listeners on every item inside a dynamically filtered list?', '', '["CSS forbids per-item clicks","One parent listener handles dynamic items cleanly without duplicate listener leaks","It bypasses CORS"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Delegated listeners survive list re-renders without rebinding overhead.'),
  ('ff467300-3c2c-e95e-c1ad-f1fe14ac7bc2'::uuid, '1ae9367d-03f1-bec6-d004-742aa7467bb9'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'When auditing a layout overflowing horizontally on a 375px phone, what flex property commonly resolves long child stretching?', '', '["min-width: 0 with flex-wrap: wrap","z-index: 999","position: fixed"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'min-width: 0 lets flex children shrink below intrinsic text width cleanly.'),
  ('a39cbe6a-05ec-3544-7ef4-01e65750cf85'::uuid, '1ae9367d-03f1-bec6-d004-742aa7467bb9'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'In a bug triage workflow, why is catching an API error and silently returning [] harmful?', '', '["Uses extra RAM","It conceals real backend/schema failures behind fake empty states","Slows localStorage"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Surfacing explicit errors enables diagnosing and fixing root defects immediately.'),
  ('4c459fa4-a286-9fee-e4de-d195c28ea1d0'::uuid, '1ae9367d-03f1-bec6-d004-742aa7467bb9'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'What distinguishes high-signal engineering pull requests from noisy ones?', '', '["No description needed","Clear why, trade-offs, scoped diff, and explicit verification evidence","50+ unrelated files"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Focused diffs paired with verification context catch edge cases fast.'),
  ('a7a541c4-8ebe-2e83-207c-269b2630c65c'::uuid, '1ae9367d-03f1-bec6-d004-742aa7467bb9'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why define explicit binary acceptance criteria on tickets prior to coding?', '', '["Satisfies HR quotas","Aligns engineering and QA on exact verifiable Done conditions upfront","Replaces version control"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Clear Done criteria prevent scope creep and rework cycles.'),
  ('a9b21d7b-e16d-bd04-a741-1065defe73b0'::uuid, 'b0d53e95-8bd9-d23b-8999-c59a01778c8b'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'When does a relational schema require a dedicated junction table like course_skills?', '', '["For 1:1 profile extensions","When modeling many-to-many relationships with clean foreign keys and indexes","When storing plain text descriptions"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Junction tables normalize M:N links cleanly with composite keys and FKs.'),
  ('f1ceebf1-487a-6f46-2928-c8522f2407f7'::uuid, 'b0d53e95-8bd9-d23b-8999-c59a01778c8b'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'When both a direct FK (courses.skill_id) and junction table (course_skills) link two tables, how do you fix PostgREST ambiguous embed errors?', '', '["Drop the junction table","Qualify the embed explicitly with the exact FK constraint name (e.g. skills!courses_skill_id_fkey)","Return empty arrays on error"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit FK hints distinguish primary vs secondary relationships without losing data.'),
  ('bbda828d-1299-4c57-8634-330997f9650b'::uuid, 'b0d53e95-8bd9-d23b-8999-c59a01778c8b'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why must answer_config and correct_index columns on public.questions be revoked from authenticated SELECT grants?', '', '["Saves bandwidth","Prevents learners from reading exam answers directly via REST API prior to grading","Improves CSS render speed"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Column-level grants protect assessment integrity at the database boundary.'),
  ('15933bcf-896e-798c-def6-cd87ee3deabd'::uuid, 'b0d53e95-8bd9-d23b-8999-c59a01778c8b'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What prevents double-clicks or network retries from creating duplicate quiz attempts or submissions?', '', '["Longer CSS animations","Unique (user_id, idempotency_key) constraints and transactional checks","Hiding console logs"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Database uniqueness guarantees exact idempotency under concurrent requests.'),
  ('b46639bb-7f02-411b-c040-5c4db05861f9'::uuid, 'b0d53e95-8bd9-d23b-8999-c59a01778c8b'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'How should first production administrators be provisioned in Supabase?', '', '["Hardcoded email auto-promotion trigger","Explicit service_role invocation of admin_assign_profile_role after standard signup","Frontend localStorage toggle"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Service-role-only promotion with audit logging avoids hardcoded privilege targets.'),
  ('55de4fb0-6ef2-a16d-f0b2-84359567db4a'::uuid, '00d53ee2-030a-c772-4ce3-a5b8b444a5ba'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What is the N+1 query anti-pattern?', '', '["Running 1 query per parent row inside a loop after fetching N parents","Using PostgreSQL UUIDs","Writing parameterized $1 queries"]'::jsonb, 0, '{}'::jsonb, 'Looping per-row queries slows endpoints dramatically compared to JOINs or batched fetches.'),
  ('01706919-635d-8830-e8c0-c8407a43d14f'::uuid, '00d53ee2-030a-c772-4ce3-a5b8b444a5ba'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why enforce timed quiz expiration via server-side quiz_sessions rather than client JS timers?', '', '["JS lacks Date objects","Clients can pause or tamper with browser timers; server clocks enforce true elapsed limits","CSS animations reset timers"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Server timestamps keep timed assessments tamper-resistant.'),
  ('fc6b0d6e-69e2-3ecb-5675-235bb52f119f'::uuid, '00d53ee2-030a-c772-4ce3-a5b8b444a5ba'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What must happen if a client uploads a file to private storage and the subsequent submission RPC throws an error?', '', '["Leave file forever","Attempt compensating storage object cleanup so orphan files do not accumulate","Disable storage RLS"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Compensating cleanup keeps storage and DB consistent.'),
  ('6dec851d-09bd-0997-45d4-4d39641e06d0'::uuid, '00d53ee2-030a-c772-4ce3-a5b8b444a5ba'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why should production frontend builds fail closed when Supabase env vars are missing?', '', '["Faster Vite bundling","Prevents production users from silently landing in local fake Demo Mode","Avoids CORS headers"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Fail-closed configuration catches broken deployment config safely.'),
  ('827ee56e-ee77-7a55-c8e7-a5eea93c352c'::uuid, '00d53ee2-030a-c772-4ce3-a5b8b444a5ba'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'What makes database migrations safe for active production systems?', '', '["Editing old applied SQL files in place","Additive, idempotent forward-only migrations preserving legitimate existing rows","Running TRUNCATE before seed"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Forward-only additive migrations evolve schemas without destroying data.'),
  ('7af7f31b-1005-5fdd-af98-ceaa81162bfc'::uuid, '00d53ee2-030a-c772-4ce3-a5b8b444a5ba'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Which combination verifies backend database security most reliably in automated tests?', '', '["Mocking fetch() only","Running migrations against real PostgreSQL/PGlite and simulating anon, learner, and admin actors","Visual screenshot diffing"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Real SQL execution catches RLS, grant, trigger, and constraint bugs directly.'),
  ('c442009c-00d7-a698-ff24-60de54358ebb'::uuid, '58e10950-2fb4-c409-5d64-6cebfa9cf7df'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What is the recommended minimum touch target size for mobile buttons and links?', '', '["18x18px","44x44 CSS px (48dp) with adequate spacing","100% screen width always"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, '44x44px+ hit areas drastically reduce mobile mis-taps.'),
  ('a5159f2e-e734-235a-43c1-d916e662164d'::uuid, '58e10950-2fb4-c409-5d64-6cebfa9cf7df'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why reserve fixed container heights or aspect-ratios for async mobile card thumbnails?', '', '["Increases download speed","Prevents Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) jumping under tapping fingers","Enables offline storage"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit container boxes keep layout geometry stable during image load.'),
  ('702b1f19-5153-7b0a-fd12-27dc5b3f1f36'::uuid, '58e10950-2fb4-c409-5d64-6cebfa9cf7df'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'In Boundary Value Analysis, why test both 69% and 70% around a 70% pass cutoff?', '', '["Tests CSS transitions","Catches off-by-one comparison bugs (> vs >=) right on the threshold","Required by HTTP"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Boundary values catch subtle comparison bugs immediately.'),
  ('c91fe69d-3d6f-3455-0608-ea495f86eb08'::uuid, '58e10950-2fb4-c409-5d64-6cebfa9cf7df'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why avoid arbitrary sleep() delays inside automated test suites?', '', '["Fails browser CSS","Makes suites slow and intermittently flaky on varying CI CPU loads","Disables assertions"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit promise awaits and injected timestamps are fast and deterministic.'),
  ('0f54a947-c1db-943c-b51b-258f5ee5c13c'::uuid, '58e10950-2fb4-c409-5d64-6cebfa9cf7df'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'If a mobile POST request times out on weak transit Wi-Fi, what should the UI do?', '', '["Wipe form fields","Preserve user input cleanly, surface clear retry feedback, and reuse the idempotency key","Sign the user out"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Preserving drafts plus idempotent retries prevents lost work and duplicate saves.'),
  ('4fa7fc30-b5bd-27cd-96c0-b900b0d60f52'::uuid, '83ea5df2-b3e0-5fd9-1f0a-1fd883d8d586'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'How do you make screen-reader announcements accurate on an icon-only Show/Hide password button?', '', '["Use CSS ::before text","Toggle aria-pressed (\"true\"/\"false\") and descriptive aria-label dynamically","Hide button with opacity: 0"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Dynamic ARIA attributes communicate current state cleanly to assistive tools.'),
  ('c43120d7-a922-c794-b6f3-8d6603b3e641'::uuid, '83ea5df2-b3e0-5fd9-1f0a-1fd883d8d586'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'What is the core risk of mocking away database constraints and permissions in every test?', '', '["Slows unit runs","False greens hide broken SQL queries, RLS lockouts, and schema mismatches","Breaks localStorage"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Real DB/contract tests verify actual backend integration boundaries.'),
  ('56f26c7e-3ad6-cce6-cb01-d7aa1bd6581e'::uuid, '83ea5df2-b3e0-5fd9-1f0a-1fd883d8d586'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'When is the best moment for a mobile app to prompt for notification or camera permissions?', '', '["Cold app splash screen","Right when the user triggers a relevant feature explaining the direct benefit","During sign-out"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Contextual prompts maximize user trust and grant rates.'),
  ('21711f8f-4e51-07c8-dc1c-8bf18ccf60f7'::uuid, '83ea5df2-b3e0-5fd9-1f0a-1fd883d8d586'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Which ordering of CI pipeline checks gives engineers fastest feedback?', '', '["Slow E2E first -> lint last","Fast static lint/checkJs -> unit & DB integration tests -> build -> smoke checks","Deploy first -> lint later"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Fast static checks catch syntax and import errors within seconds.'),
  ('b619c192-170b-a224-7042-8c1a0071215d'::uuid, '83ea5df2-b3e0-5fd9-1f0a-1fd883d8d586'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'What information makes a QA bug report immediately actionable?', '', '["\"Doesn’t work\" screenshot only","Mode/role, numbered repro steps, observed network/console error, and expected behavior","Number of lines changed"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Exact repro conditions and raw error payloads eliminate diagnostic guesswork.'),
  ('ab566270-ff2f-cee6-f0ee-8d8392481dfc'::uuid, '83ea5df2-b3e0-5fd9-1f0a-1fd883d8d586'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'How do you ensure a fixed bug cannot silently return in later code edits?', '', '["Add a TODO comment","Write an automated regression test failing before the fix and passing after","Disable CI checks"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Automated regression tests enforce solved behaviors permanently.'),
  ('11f8ec84-d337-9899-2167-c2c569caf034'::uuid, '58d6a682-7d61-bb68-b2ce-e67dbf37cad4'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What prevents IDOR (Insecure Direct Object Reference) vulnerabilities?', '', '["Random-looking CSS IDs","Enforcing server-derived caller identity and row ownership/RLS on every target ID","Client-side route guards"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Server/DB ownership checks stop tampered ID access regardless of URL structure.'),
  ('8021a4e2-9983-2a62-b59f-054fe59bcb2e'::uuid, '58d6a682-7d61-bb68-b2ce-e67dbf37cad4'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why must service_role keys NEVER appear inside VITE_* variables or src/ files?', '', '["Vite strips underscores","service_role bypasses all RLS and VITE_* vars are compiled into public browser JS","Slows HMR"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Browser bundles are public to any user inspecting network/source.'),
  ('18686f75-5fe0-5bf3-d8ae-55c87402ee42'::uuid, '58d6a682-7d61-bb68-b2ce-e67dbf37cad4'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why use private storage buckets with short-lived signed URLs for user submissions?', '', '["Increases upload limits","Prevents unauthorized public enumeration or hotlinking of private learner files","Avoids CORS headers"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Signed URLs authorize each temporary read cleanly.'),
  ('19016673-5572-40e5-9a04-06390a15ea21'::uuid, '58d6a682-7d61-bb68-b2ce-e67dbf37cad4'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What is the safest fix if an app query throws a Supabase/PostgREST relationship or permission error?', '', '["Turn off RLS","Fix the query foreign-key hint or add legitimate narrow RPC/policy logic","Promote all users to admin"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Fix root query/contract issues without weakening database security.'),
  ('3b62e216-dbc5-1ac8-6ca2-4eb08fc92b6c'::uuid, '58d6a682-7d61-bb68-b2ce-e67dbf37cad4'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'In technical incident triage, why verify active environment mode first?', '', '["Improves Tailwind styles","Prevents confusing local dev demo fixtures with live Supabase accounts","Speeds DNS"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Confirming target environment prevents misdiagnosing cross-mode auth errors.'),
  ('ec64e013-acd5-057b-be02-4f7a2ebd1ede'::uuid, 'b6ca543e-c04e-d59c-19d9-23bad4920f9f'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Which mechanism makes sensitive admin operations accountable even if reviewed months later?', '', '["Console.log statements","Append-only admin_audit_logs table capturing actor, action, target, and before/after diffs with UPDATE/DELETE blocked","Browser cookies"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Immutable audit logs preserve non-repudiable operational history.'),
  ('48ae7f1c-1145-8d11-23e7-232ae1b871ad'::uuid, 'b6ca543e-c04e-d59c-19d9-23bad4920f9f'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why should CI pipelines run `npm ci` against a committed `package-lock.json`?', '', '["Installs React automatically","Guarantees reproducible exact dependency trees and fails if lockfile drifts","Bypasses Vite"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'npm ci locks production builds to audited exact dependency versions.'),
  ('11d569d8-9987-5460-6151-644bfd1539bd'::uuid, 'b6ca543e-c04e-d59c-19d9-23bad4920f9f'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why validate uploaded file magic bytes and server-side storage metadata in addition to filename extensions?', '', '["Faster thumbnails","Extensions can be trivially renamed to disguise executables or active HTML/SVG payloads","Browsers require PNGs"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Content/MIME inspection stops disguised malicious file uploads.'),
  ('5f394ed3-9aa0-93cb-f979-3b8d75f219fd'::uuid, 'b6ca543e-c04e-d59c-19d9-23bad4920f9f'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What is the priority immediate action when a bad code deploy breaks production requests?', '', '["Edit production JS files via SSH","Rollback cleanly to the last known-good build first, then diagnose and add a regression test","Turn off monitoring"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Instant rollback minimizes user outage time safely.'),
  ('e5d8cf6d-4438-295c-43c8-0c2b77ed127b'::uuid, 'b6ca543e-c04e-d59c-19d9-23bad4920f9f'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Why must support staff never ask users for their passwords during login troubleshooting?', '', '["Emails strip symbols","Sharing credentials compromises user security; use reset flows and safe server diagnostics instead","Slows database indexes"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Password resets and server logs diagnose login issues safely without credential exposure.'),
  ('37c80021-2695-775d-3bcc-2aaf28566d7a'::uuid, 'b6ca543e-c04e-d59c-19d9-23bad4920f9f'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'How does keeping dependencies minimal help cybersecurity?', '', '["Eliminates need for HTTPS","Reduces transitive vulnerability surface, audit noise, and bundle bloat","Disables SQL injection"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Smaller audited dependency trees minimize attack surface cleanly.'),
  ('6892da9f-e031-5cbd-bf24-1eec2204fe6e'::uuid, '57caca15-6d48-8084-d035-280bcc397bc6'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What is the safest way to inspect total study minutes when joining courses with a many-to-many course_skills table?', '', '["Multiply by 2","Aggregate or deduplicate by unique lesson/user before joining multi-skill links","Ignore course_skills"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Joining M:N links before summing duplicates rows and inflates metrics.'),
  ('b09268b3-c3da-fa3e-e016-e83c547f3bdf'::uuid, '57caca15-6d48-8084-d035-280bcc397bc6'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'When analyzing heavily skewed duration or salary data, why include the median?', '', '["Replaces sample size","Extreme outliers pull the mean far above typical experience","Eliminates nulls"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Median captures central tendency accurately under skew.'),
  ('9ef1b78a-0441-b5da-15b6-6049732dbcf3'::uuid, '57caca15-6d48-8084-d035-280bcc397bc6'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why instruct extraction prompts to state "Not found in source" when evidence is missing?', '', '["Reduces token cost","Curtails confident AI hallucinations/fabrications","Disables JSON"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit abstention permissions cut invented claims dramatically.'),
  ('cef258c6-0c28-116a-61e0-a4035988cc65'::uuid, '57caca15-6d48-8084-d035-280bcc397bc6'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What defines target (data) leakage in supervised machine learning?', '', '["Slow CSV loading","Training features containing information unavailable at real prediction time","Missing CSS rules"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Future/post-outcome features inflate offline scores while failing live predictions.'),
  ('6e46de93-51ff-8b3f-db67-b837ab5ae99f'::uuid, '57caca15-6d48-8084-d035-280bcc397bc6'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Why can’t observational correlation between two metrics prove causation automatically?', '', '["SQL lacks division","Hidden confounding variables or self-selection may explain both metrics","Pie charts hide trends"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Confounders must be ruled out via experiments or careful study design.'),
  ('4d148a47-8e6e-7931-fea3-82a874e0f8b4'::uuid, 'a1814372-d8c1-15f7-879d-577dfd665294'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'On a dataset with 99% healthy items and 1% defects, why is 99% raw accuracy deceptive?', '', '["Colors look muted","Predicting \"all healthy\" hits 99% accuracy while catching 0% of real defects","Median drops to zero"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Imbalanced datasets require Precision, Recall, and confusion matrix inspection.'),
  ('11da1cec-f888-a327-f8f0-1426980dfa5a'::uuid, 'a1814372-d8c1-15f7-879d-577dfd665294'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Which error metric prioritizes catching as many real positive/at-risk cases as possible?', '', '["Precision","Recall (Sensitivity)","R-squared"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Recall measures fraction of true positives successfully captured.'),
  ('40fdc841-3435-d5f3-ca06-5f852fc9a936'::uuid, 'a1814372-d8c1-15f7-879d-577dfd665294'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'How must data scaling and imputation medians be computed in ML pipelines?', '', '["Across full Train + Test combined","Fit strictly on Train split only, then transform Validation/Test cleanly","Hardcode zero everywhere"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Fitting preprocessing on Test data leaks held-out evaluation distribution.'),
  ('e43219c8-5d80-6764-c25a-4c084dc827d1'::uuid, 'a1814372-d8c1-15f7-879d-577dfd665294'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What makes indirect prompt injection risky when processing external resumes or web pages?', '', '["Breaks UTF-8","Hidden untrusted text can override instructions unless outputs face deterministic checks and human review","Slows DNS"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Untrusted input text must never drive unchecked automated approvals.'),
  ('b372cb96-d15c-6c48-3613-890f97063ec1'::uuid, 'a1814372-d8c1-15f7-879d-577dfd665294'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Why must bar charts start their numeric axis at zero?', '', '["Prevents browser crash","Non-zero baselines visually distort small differences into misleading giant gaps","Required for JSON"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Proportional bar visual comparison requires a true zero baseline.'),
  ('dc1935c1-c9e7-8ad3-c824-a8b53a6673ce'::uuid, 'a1814372-d8c1-15f7-879d-577dfd665294'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What separates an effective team AI policy from vague bans?', '', '["50 pages of legalese","Clear rules on PII redaction, mandatory factual/test verification, and human accountability","No code reviews"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Actionable privacy and verification rules enable safe productivity.'),
  ('81320320-eb3a-638e-9170-9ff7ff7f01d0'::uuid, '9dc8cda3-3ddd-e31e-de01-0cbc48d6de63'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What formula transforms weak CV duty statements into strong impact bullets?', '', '["Adjective + Role Title","Action Verb + Specific Scope/Tools + Measurable or Concrete Outcome","Responsibilities copied from job ad"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Action + context + result proves real contribution quickly.'),
  ('4bf4e693-90c9-df8a-c843-305c30358b2e'::uuid, '9dc8cda3-3ddd-e31e-de01-0cbc48d6de63'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'Why test your exported CV PDF by copy-pasting into a plain text editor?', '', '["Checks file size","Verifies ATS parsers and screen readers follow clean reading order without column scrambling","Adds hyperlinks"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Plain-text copy confirms layout structure parses cleanly.'),
  ('47352dd8-bd58-ed47-560b-89dc995c3cab'::uuid, '9dc8cda3-3ddd-e31e-de01-0cbc48d6de63'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Which portfolio curation strategy impresses hiring managers most?', '', '["20 unannotated tutorial clones","2–4 complete case studies detailing Problem, Your Role, Process, and Verified Outcome","Screenshots without links"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Curated case studies prove problem-solving judgment and execution.'),
  ('0ce9a829-9a83-1a9c-f5f3-4ba0e76ba23b'::uuid, '9dc8cda3-3ddd-e31e-de01-0cbc48d6de63'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'In STAR interview storytelling, what share of time belongs on your specific Action?', '', '["5%","Roughly 60% focusing clearly on what YOU decided and executed","90% background context"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Interviewers hire based on how you analyze and act under constraints.'),
  ('b6954a35-a106-2a9f-130b-59823e1830d3'::uuid, '9dc8cda3-3ddd-e31e-de01-0cbc48d6de63'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Why check every portfolio link inside an incognito browser before applying?', '', '["Boosts download speed","Exposes private permission walls, expired logins, and 404 errors external reviewers would hit","Tests dark mode"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Logged-out testing guarantees friction-free reviewer access.'),
  ('2ede5506-04c8-0cc2-6b5f-605b2e5aef26'::uuid, '8e0d2128-c6b5-bd8c-8fd5-0c95b79021a2'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What defines a T-shaped career skill strategy?', '', '["Learning 12 unrelated topics superficially","Deep verified craft in one core skill paired with collaborative fluency in adjacent areas","Avoiding communication skills"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Deep anchor mastery plus adjacent fluency makes contributors versatile and rare.'),
  ('8cff1335-720a-95dd-9e5d-907ebcaef6a0'::uuid, '8e0d2128-c6b5-bd8c-8fd5-0c95b79021a2'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'What makes warm/cold outreach messages significantly more likely to earn replies?', '', '["Sending 500-word bios daily","Short (<100 words), personalized shared context, relevant proof, and a low-friction ask","Attaching unrequested ZIP files"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Respectful brevity plus relevance stands out in busy inboxes.'),
  ('6ddc57bf-c20b-9b66-973e-3f3bf6b04832'::uuid, '8e0d2128-c6b5-bd8c-8fd5-0c95b79021a2'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'How should you respond when asked in an interview about a significant mistake?', '', '["Blame former teammates","Own the error clearly without excuses and highlight the process/check you built to prevent repeats","Claim zero mistakes ever"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Accountability and systemic learning demonstrate real maturity.'),
  ('137be726-9e3c-2917-f7e0-4056e55a7623'::uuid, '8e0d2128-c6b5-bd8c-8fd5-0c95b79021a2'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What should a candidate do before accepting or negotiating a written job offer?', '', '["Reject instantly for practice","Review total scope, manager fit, ask 24–48h thoughtfully, and negotiate calmly around shared value","Reply only with emojis"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Calm, collaborative review ensures sound long-term alignment.'),
  ('c9b6d7ae-567d-d32b-6d55-b58f3ee54a70'::uuid, '8e0d2128-c6b5-bd8c-8fd5-0c95b79021a2'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'During your first 30 days in a new role, which habit builds fastest team trust?', '', '["Demanding full rewrites on Day 2","Listening curiously, fixing onboarding doc friction, and shipping clean small wins reliably","Working silently without check-ins"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Curious learning plus reliable small execution earns trust immediately.'),
  ('1bd731bd-2fc0-f514-c22c-6c802e30b0fe'::uuid, '8e0d2128-c6b5-bd8c-8fd5-0c95b79021a2'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why maintain an ongoing monthly "Win / Evidence Document" throughout your career?', '', '["Replaces version control","Preserves exact metrics, deliverables, and feedback for effortless reviews, negotiations, and CV updates","Avoids portfolio projects"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Real-time win logs prevent forgetting high-impact contributions months later.'),
  ('a0e0c8a2-7404-e93b-a216-a06818870223'::uuid, '55965a83-bb97-afb4-3b28-d0be2ae70c4e'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What makes a remote message follow the "No Hello" async principle?', '', '["Starting with \"Hey\" and waiting","Combining greeting, full question, context links, and timing inside one self-contained message","Calling without notice"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Complete messages eliminate slow multi-hour timezone ping-pong.'),
  ('5d11d8bf-6643-a3fc-115b-84a34a4f0912'::uuid, '55965a83-bb97-afb4-3b28-d0be2ae70c4e'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'When a Wednesday deadline is clearly going to slip, what builds the highest trust?', '', '["Say nothing until Wednesday evening","Alert stakeholders on Monday with current progress, honest ETA, and scope options","Silence notifications"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Early transparent escalation gives teams space to adjust calmly.'),
  ('c4470b8f-feec-e5ad-d2ca-c909a26665ec'::uuid, '55965a83-bb97-afb4-3b28-d0be2ae70c4e'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why protect peak daily energy hours for Important non-urgent work before inbox triage?', '', '["Inboxes close at noon","Urgent noise otherwise consumes the day before high-leverage priorities move forward","Emails load slower early"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Prioritizing deep important work first guarantees daily impact.'),
  ('1d65dadc-74f8-f758-ebba-bf8e978dbdb0'::uuid, '55965a83-bb97-afb4-3b28-d0be2ae70c4e'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What turns a stalled vague task ("Build Portfolio") into immediate momentum?', '', '["Buying new apps","Defining a concrete 10-minute next physical action step","Working all night"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Tiny concrete starter actions overcome initiation friction cleanly.'),
  ('9f326aad-dd7d-74a3-c592-1f7c02eb776d'::uuid, '55965a83-bb97-afb4-3b28-d0be2ae70c4e'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'Which meeting should almost always be replaced with a written update?', '', '["Sensitive team conflict resolution","Routine weekly status readouts with zero open decisions","Cross-team architecture debate"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'One-way status updates are read faster asynchronously in writing.'),
  ('3c2914de-623e-8936-9817-d533fd67b735'::uuid, 'e629acf3-e494-2d14-850e-e2d5a714b39f'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What essential step keeps remote teammates aligned right after a live decision call ends?', '', '["Nothing if recorded","Posting a 3–5 bullet Decision / Owner / Deadline wrap-up in the public project channel","Booking tomorrow’s call"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Written wrap-ups preserve shared clarity across schedules and absences.'),
  ('dc4c481d-eef2-382d-458d-83365f65b0de'::uuid, 'e629acf3-e494-2d14-850e-e2d5a714b39f'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'How should you respond initially when critical written feedback feels blunt?', '', '["Reply defensively right away","Pause briefly, assume positive intent, and ask one clarifying question focused on the artifact","Delete the project"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Artifact-centered curiosity de-escalates text ambiguity cleanly.'),
  ('b053a393-ec96-423d-38a6-13d818edccad'::uuid, 'e629acf3-e494-2d14-850e-e2d5a714b39f'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why maintain only ONE trusted task capture system with a weekly review?', '', '["Required by calendars","Stops mental anxiety over scattered commitments across apps and memory","Boosts internet speed"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'A single reviewed capture system keeps commitments visible and calm.'),
  ('faaa5eb7-ce8d-700d-8fab-b5863cfedb8f'::uuid, 'e629acf3-e494-2d14-850e-e2d5a714b39f'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What prevents remote burnout when desk and home share one space?', '', '["Always keeping chat green overnight","Using a consistent 5-min shutdown ritual, separate browser profiles, and scheduled-send bounds","Skipping lunches"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit daily boundaries protect long-term focus and wellbeing.'),
  ('0a10cb4a-09c8-533a-154c-1b82f07e62f8'::uuid, 'e629acf3-e494-2d14-850e-e2d5a714b39f'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'How can a remote contributor maintain fair visibility without noisy busyness theater?', '', '["Typing \"Online!\" at 8am","Sharing concise weekly outcome recaps, finished demo visuals, and helpful documentation","Sending hourly DMs"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Outcome-anchored recaps demonstrate real contribution across distance.'),
  ('ecbd1f5b-d2d9-8e4b-5112-67d8e5931ab3'::uuid, 'e629acf3-e494-2d14-850e-e2d5a714b39f'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why batch shallow admin chores into one afternoon block rather than doing them as pings arrive?', '', '["Improves monitor brightness","Eliminates repeated 15-minute context-switching taxes during deep focus blocks","Avoids calendars"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Batching similar shallow work protects continuous deep attention.'),
  ('19046a1d-84a6-7789-9457-d15697cfb4cf'::uuid, '24d13fbf-5353-1bf0-6d9a-77dad83ea8c9'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'What prevents unpaid scope expansion on freelance projects?', '', '["Saying \"I’m flexible!\" verbally","Listing exact deliverables, revision caps, and explicit Out-of-Scope exclusions in writing","Working without deposits"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Explicit scope boundaries prevent misunderstandings before work begins.'),
  ('a874be59-43d8-5b2c-64f9-2b67f180f333'::uuid, '24d13fbf-5353-1bf0-6d9a-77dad83ea8c9'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'When a client requests a "quick extra feature" mid-project, what is the strongest professional response?', '', '["Add it free silently","Acknowledge warmly and offer a paid Phase-2 option or equal scope swap trade-off","Stop answering emails"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Option-based responses protect margins while preserving client goodwill.'),
  ('26081336-b872-7f52-285d-6e159e1febba'::uuid, '24d13fbf-5353-1bf0-6d9a-77dad83ea8c9'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why move ~25–30% of every cleared freelance invoice immediately into a Tax Vault?', '', '["Increases credit score","Prevents spending pre-tax revenue during boom months before tax bills arrive","Avoids contracts"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Ring-fencing tax reserves protects independent cash flow cleanly.'),
  ('450eb2bb-100f-232c-8313-f411d9b4ddac'::uuid, '24d13fbf-5353-1bf0-6d9a-77dad83ea8c9'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What makes a "double opt-in" networking introduction respectful?', '', '["Sending both LinkedIn profiles publicly","Asking permission from BOTH people first before connecting them","Attaching resumes unasked"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Checking with both parties protects everyone’s calendar and privacy.'),
  ('5da2d16c-f390-dc84-5da7-3c314024ef82'::uuid, '24d13fbf-5353-1bf0-6d9a-77dad83ea8c9'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'When is the optimal time to request a client testimonial?', '', '["After a late-payment argument","Right after delivering a praised milestone or smooth project launch","Before kickoff"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Peak satisfaction produces specific, enthusiastic testimonials.'),
  ('e7b98074-d835-fe23-34fe-a879969e38f3'::uuid, '2af2370e-177c-7dbd-c93a-bf11a5b02e5f'::uuid, 1, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'How do "Hill-and-Valley" buffers stabilize irregular freelance income?', '', '["Blocks new clients","Surplus cash from high-earning months funds a steady baseline monthly draw during slow months","Eliminates invoicing"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Smoothing draws prevents overspending in peak months and panic in quiet ones.'),
  ('70b7b8f9-7ed3-caee-186a-34f45122f261'::uuid, '2af2370e-177c-7dbd-c93a-bf11a5b02e5f'::uuid, 2, 'scenario', 'medium', 1, 'What weekly client habit reduces anxious "Any update?" check-ins dramatically?', '', '["Working weekends silently","Sending a consistent Friday Done / Waiting On You / Next week update","Turning off email"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Proactive predictable status builds effortless client calm.'),
  ('c5acae71-0450-7b8d-65dc-c068f0eadbd1'::uuid, '2af2370e-177c-7dbd-c93a-bf11a5b02e5f'::uuid, 3, 'multiple_choice', 'medium', 1, 'Why factor non-billable admin, outreach, and tax time when setting freelance rates?', '', '["Makes proposals longer","Only ~60–65% of work hours are billable; rates must sustain full living and tax costs cleanly","Required by CSS"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Pricing solely at employee hourly wages underpays independent overhead severely.'),
  ('632519e6-a915-d22b-9e08-a5451c967d2b'::uuid, '2af2370e-177c-7dbd-c93a-bf11a5b02e5f'::uuid, 4, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'What turns a 1-time freelance launch into steadier monthly revenue?', '', '["Cutting rates 50%","Packaging a clear fixed-scope care retainer or repeatable productized audit for past happy clients","Ignoring past clients"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Retainers and productized offers smooth out feast-and-famine pipelines.'),
  ('bab659af-6285-4c7e-cc72-601726be4160'::uuid, '2af2370e-177c-7dbd-c93a-bf11a5b02e5f'::uuid, 5, 'multiple_choice', 'hard', 1, 'In a calm overdue-invoice follow-up sequence, what comes first at Day +1?', '', '["Threatening small-claims court","A brief, friendly check-in attaching the invoice + payment link assuming simple oversight","Deleting project files"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Friendly frictionless nudges resolve most innocent accounting delays fast.'),
  ('dc6e354f-e2d1-6732-9ada-a48e9c19188c'::uuid, '2af2370e-177c-7dbd-c93a-bf11a5b02e5f'::uuid, 6, 'scenario', 'hard', 1, 'Why refer away a project that genuinely sits outside your core craft honestly?', '', '["Reduces portfolio size","Builds deep credibility that frequently leads clients to refer ideal projects back to you","Saves PDF bytes"]'::jsonb, 1, '{}'::jsonb, 'Honest specialization strengthens long-term trust and referrals.')
on conflict (id) do update set
  quiz_id = excluded.quiz_id,
  position = excluded.position,
  question_type = excluded.question_type,
  difficulty = excluded.difficulty,
  marks = excluded.marks,
  prompt = excluded.prompt,
  context_text = excluded.context_text,
  options = excluded.options,
  correct_index = excluded.correct_index,
  answer_config = excluded.answer_config,
  explanation = excluded.explanation;

-- 12. Capstone Challenges (63)
insert into public.challenges (id, skill_id, course_id, phase_id, title, brief, instructions, expected_deliverables, submission_format, deliverable_hint, max_score, passing_score, allowed_evidence_types, allowed_mime_types, max_file_size_mb, is_required, rubric)
select v.id::uuid, sk.id, co.id, ph.id, v.title, v.brief, v.instructions, v.expected_deliverables, v.submission_format, v.deliverable_hint, v.max_score, v.passing_score, v.allowed_evidence_types, v.allowed_mime_types, v.max_file_size_mb, v.is_required, v.rubric
from (
  values
    ('d0275d62-fe57-8036-7761-b44437ba981e', 'frontend-development', 'frontend-development-foundations', null::uuid, 'Final Practical Project: Build and Deploy a Responsive Business Website', 'Design, code, and deploy a multi-section responsive website for a real or fictional local business using semantic HTML5, responsive CSS (Flexbox & Grid), interactive DOM controls, and a validated contact/inquiry form.', 'Include at least 3 pages or 4 distinct sections (Hero, Services Grid, Interactive FAQ/Filter, Validated Inquiry Form), verify mobile responsiveness at 375px and desktop at 1440px, and publish to a live static host (GitHub Pages, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, or Vercel).', '["Live deployed HTTPS website URL","Public Git repository link showing clean HTML/CSS/JS files","Screenshot or brief architecture & accessibility audit notes (focus order, contrast, and responsive breakpoints)"]'::jsonb, 'Live project URL + Git repository URL + optional screenshot/notes', 'Submit your deployed URL, Git repo URL, and explain how you tested responsiveness and form validation.', 25, 18, '["project_url","repo_url","screenshot","file","written"]'::jsonb, '["image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","application/pdf","application/zip"]'::jsonb, 20, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Semantic HTML5 & Accessibility","description":"Valid landmarks, single h1, labelled form inputs, keyboard focus visibility.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Responsive CSS Architecture","description":"Clean Flexbox/Grid layout across mobile (375px) and desktop (1440px) with zero horizontal overflow.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"JavaScript Interactivity & Validation","description":"Working DOM interactions (e.g. filter/FAQ) and friendly inline form validation without console errors.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Live Deployment & Code Organisation","description":"Working HTTPS URL with relative asset paths and clean file structure.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('1d619738-ed90-b833-09f7-280c491ce91d', 'graphic-design', 'graphic-design-foundations', null::uuid, 'Final Practical Project: Produce an Original Promotional Flyer for a Fictional Business', 'Design an original A5 or US Letter promotional flyer for a fictional local business or event, applying your brand sheet, 60-30-10 palette, paired typography, grid alignment, and clear call-to-action.', 'Include a clear headline, focal visual or illustration, offer/event details (date, venue, offer, CTA), and generous margins. Export as a crisp PNG/JPG preview or print-ready PDF and explain your typography, palette, and grid decisions.', '["Original promotional flyer file (PDF, PNG, JPG, or WebP)","Design rationale detailing target audience, font pairing, 60-30-10 colour values, and grid margins"]'::jsonb, 'Flyer upload (PDF/PNG/JPG/WebP) or public Figma/Canva share link + written rationale', 'Upload your promotional flyer (PDF/PNG/JPG, max 20 MB) or share a link, and explain your design choices.', 25, 18, '["file","screenshot","project_url","written"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp"]'::jsonb, 20, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Visual Hierarchy & 3-Second Read","description":"Unmistakable focal headline, clear offer details, and prominent CTA.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Typography & Grid Alignment","description":"Max 2 fonts, balanced scale contrast, clean alignment, and generous outer margins.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Colour Contrast & Brand Fit","description":"Cohesive 60-30-10 palette with legible >= 4.5:1 text contrast.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Production Polish & Rationale","description":"Clean export quality, zero clipped elements, and clear explanation of decisions.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('c0835f0e-6a94-6eee-ab76-ecedb36338b4', 'digital-marketing-fundamentals', 'digital-marketing-foundations', null::uuid, 'Final Practical Project: Develop a Seven-Day Integrated Marketing Campaign', 'Plan and draft a complete 7-day marketing campaign for a real or fictional product/service, connecting audience research, daily channel deliverables, copywriting, UTM tracking, and optimisation KPIs.', 'Include: (1) Target audience ICP + core value proposition, (2) Day 1–7 channel calendar (Social, Email, and Paid/Landing touchpoints), (3) At least 2 complete copy deliverables (1 PAS email + 2 social posts), (4) Standardised UTM link plan, and (5) Primary KPIs + 1 Day-8 A/B test plan.', '["Complete 7-day campaign plan (submitted directly as structured text, PDF/DOCX/CSV upload, or public Notion/Docs link)","Target audience profile, copy deliverables, UTM schema, and success metrics"]'::jsonb, 'Written campaign blueprint, PDF/DOCX/CSV upload, or shared document link', 'Paste your 7-day campaign plan directly or upload a PDF/DOCX/CSV document with your UTM table and copy drafts.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/csv","text/plain","image/png","image/jpeg"]'::jsonb, 20, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Audience Alignment & Value Proposition","description":"Clear ICP triggers, objections, and coherent offer positioning.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r2","label":"7-Day Sequencing & Copy Quality","description":"Logical multi-day arc with specific, outcome-driven copy and clear CTAs.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r3","label":"UTM Hygiene & Measurement Plan","description":"Consistent UTM links and actionable funnel KPIs (CTR, CVR, CPA).","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Optimisation Readiness","description":"Concrete post-launch diagnostic thresholds and A/B test hypothesis.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('1499f3ea-3553-be49-09f5-1dc9d659c4e0', 'public-speaking', 'communication-and-public-speaking', null::uuid, 'Final Practical Project: Record a Structured Two-Minute Presentation with Outline and Reflection', 'Prepare and record an original 2-minute presentation (~1:45–2:15) on a topic relevant to your career or community, and submit your recording alongside your speech outline and 3-pass self-reflection.', 'Deliver a clear 15-second hook, 3 structured main points, and a deliberate closing call-to-action. Upload an audio or video recording (or private/unlisted video URL) plus paste your keyword outline and written reflection covering strengths and next rehearsal goals.', '["2-minute audio or video recording (MP4, WebM, MP3, WAV, M4A, or hosted link)","Structured presentation outline (Hook, 3 Pillars, Closing CTA)","Written 3-pass reflection evaluating vocal pacing, non-verbal delivery, and audience clarity"]'::jsonb, 'Audio/Video upload (MP4/WebM/MP3/WAV, max 50 MB) or presentation link + written outline & reflection', 'Attach your 2-minute audio/video file (or unlisted video link) and include your outline & reflection in the text boxes below.', 25, 18, '["audio","video","project_url","file","written"]'::jsonb, '["video/mp4","video/webm","video/quicktime","audio/mpeg","audio/wav","audio/mp4","audio/webm","audio/ogg","application/pdf"]'::jsonb, 50, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Presentation Structure & Timing","description":"Crisp opening hook, 3 clear pillars, strong closing CTA, ~2 minutes total.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Vocal Clarity, Pacing & Pauses","description":"Steady conversational speed, natural emphasis, minimal fillers, clean audio.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Presence & Audience Framing","description":"Direct eye/camera engagement, grounded posture, and audience-relevant examples.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Outline Quality & Honest Self-Reflection","description":"Clean keyword outline paired with concrete 3-pass observations.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('59d25aeb-9d07-d5b6-7bbd-3c84017f645d', 'effective-communication', 'effective-communication-foundations', '9e7cc624-a318-9ddd-2e23-e383c443751b'::uuid, 'Workplace Communication Alignment Pack', 'Produce a complete 3-part workplace communication pack for a realistic cross-functional scenario: (1) a decision-ready stakeholder update email, (2) a difficult trade-off / feedback script using SBI and Yes-If framing, and (3) a 25-minute meeting agenda with a Decisions, Owners, and Dates (DOD) recap.', 'Pick a realistic multi-team delay or scope conflict (e.g., missed vendor asset, shifting launch scope, or conflicting stakeholder feedback). Draft all three deliverables in crisp, scannable prose showing audience framing, clear next actions, and empathetic tone.', '["Part 1: Scannable BLUF stakeholder update email (with explicit recommendation and decision ask)","Part 2: Peer SBI feedback script + \"Yes, if...\" timeline trade-off conversation script","Part 3: Focused 25-minute alignment agenda + completed DOD recap log"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written response or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all three communication artifacts cleanly labelled, or upload your PDF/DOCX pack.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Audience Framing & BLUF Clarity","description":"Main decision, impact, and concrete ask appear clearly in opening lines.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Tone, Empathy & SBI Precision","description":"Non-defensive language, observable behaviors, and realistic trade-off options.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Scannable Formatting & Channel Fit","description":"Visual hierarchy, tight paragraphs, and appropriate async vs. live structure.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Actionability & DOD Accountability","description":"Unambiguous owners, deliverable definitions, and explicit milestone dates.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('f6754e54-5988-b4ac-1166-f2895677b06d', 'business-communication', 'business-communication-essentials', '1c2a48b9-5bbe-513c-352d-bc8371c6b71f'::uuid, 'Executive Briefing & Business Comms Portfolio', 'Prepare a 3-document executive communication suite for a mid-quarter launch adjustment: (1) a 1-page BLUF Business Case / Adjustment Memo requesting £3,500 emergency tooling or contractor allocation, (2) a weekly Amber RAG Stakeholder Status Digest, and (3) a transparent Client/Partner Delay Notice + internal escalation note.', 'Ensure all figures, dates, owners, and trade-offs align consistently across the three documents. Avoid vague adjectives, passive voice, or buried asks.', '["Document 1: 1-Page BLUF Business Case with payback math & Risks/Mitigations matrix","Document 2: Weekly Amber RAG Digest with Action Headlines and DOD next steps","Document 3: Transparent Client Schedule Update & No-Surprise Escalation Note"]'::jsonb, 'Combined written submission or uploaded PDF/DOCX/Markdown pack', 'Submit your three aligned business documents cleanly labelled by section.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"BLUF & Decision Clarity","description":"Actionable headline recommendation, owner, and deadline upfront in every doc.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Commercial & Metric Reasoning","description":"Logical cost/payback framing and insight-led RAG metrics without spin.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Stakeholder & Scope Professionalism","description":"Constructive options, non-defensive escalation, and credible mitigations.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Executive Writing Polish","description":"Active voice, tight scannable structure, zero hedges, and full consistency.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('e2bf220e-5344-841f-6cac-a80e1be75e65', 'professional-communication', 'professional-workplace-communication', '28fedb46-1926-6e1b-faf4-d14cce6c628f'::uuid, 'Workplace Professionalism & Scenario Response Kit', 'Respond cleanly to four realistic workplace scenarios in one coherent portfolio: (1) turning a messy Slack thread into a respectful bundled update + 1:1 manager briefing note, (2) writing a composed error disclosure & prevention email after shipping flawed numbers, (3) drafting a courteous leave handover card, and (4) scripting a calm response to critical feedback.', 'Write each artifact ready to send in a real company. Maintain neutral warmth, active ownership, zero passive-aggressive cues, and crystal-clear dates/owners.', '["Scenario 1: Bundled async request + concise Manager 1:1 Briefing Agenda","Scenario 2: Transparent Error Disclosure & Prevention Guardrail Email","Scenario 3: 1-Page Out-of-Office Coverage & Fallback Brief","Scenario 4: Composed Critical Feedback Response & Follow-Up Plan"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written response or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Complete all four scenarios clearly in the submission editor or upload a PDF/DOCX document.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Tone, Etiquette & Generosity","description":"Warm, calm, non-defensive digital tone minus passive-aggressive cues.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Accountability & Error Recovery","description":"Honest ownership minus blame plus concrete system prevention steps.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Upward Clarity & Coverage Structure","description":"Crisp scannable 1:1 options and clear OOO fallback contacts.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Actionability & Channel Discipline","description":"Single-bubble requests, clear timestamps, and zero vague asks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('56517af5-3940-e813-c480-8e37f51501c8', 'negotiation-skills', 'negotiation-skills-deal-craft', 'e74fd32c-a957-b765-5baf-1aeff7e84359'::uuid, 'Multi-Issue Negotiation Brief & Deal Closure Pack', 'Build a complete end-to-end negotiation playbook for either (a) a £7,500 multi-month client retainer OR (b) a mid-level full-time role offer negotiation. Include: (1) full BATNA/ZOPA/Interests preparation matrix, (2) 3-option MESO proposal grid, (3) lowball & late-nibble response scripts, and (4) same-day written agreement confirmation email.', 'Ensure numbers, scope adjustments, conditional "If...then" trades, and client/employer review SLAs are consistent across all four components.', '["Part 1: Negotiation Prep Matrix (BATNA, floor, target, counterparty interests)","Part 2: 3-Option MESO Proposal Table keeping margin intact","Part 3: Lowball Counter + Late-Nibble Diplomatic Response Scripts","Part 4: Same-Day Agreement Confirmation Summary Email"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written response or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four negotiation components clearly structured in text or uploaded file.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"BATNA, ZOPA & Interest Mapping","description":"Realistic fallback option, concrete reservation line, and clear non-price interests.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"MESO Design & Conditional Trades","description":"Three balanced options with crisp \"If...then\" conditional concessions.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Tactic Handling & Poise","description":"Constructive re-anchoring and scope-rate protection against lowballs/nibbles.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Written Agreement Precision","description":"Complete same-day recap covering deliverables, dates, SLAs, and boundaries.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('14e018d5-6185-c57a-7b33-0d9d2219f847', 'persuasion-and-influence', 'ethical-persuasion-stakeholder-influence', 'b56af6ea-350e-518b-279a-81eb4acfa578'::uuid, 'Ethical Influence & Coalition Change Package', 'Develop a complete persuasive campaign to secure voluntary cross-functional adoption for a practical workplace or community change initiative without relying on formal authority. Include: (1) 4-stakeholder KPI/Fear map, (2) 2 tailored evidence-and-story pitches for contrasting audiences, (3) a Pre-Wiring Outreach & Objection Q&A plan, and (4) a 30-day friction-free adoption plan.', 'Ground your case in realistic numbers, honest trade-offs, local pilot strategy, and autonomy-respecting closing asks.', '["Part 1: 4-Stakeholder Incentives, Fears & Native KPI Map","Part 2: Two Tailored Value-Framed Pitches (combining Ethos/Pathos/Logos)","Part 3: Pre-Wiring Sequence & 4-Objection Diagnostic Q&A","Part 4: 30-Day Reversible Pilot & Friction-Removal Adoption Plan"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written response or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four parts cleanly labelled showing honest trade-offs and pilot safeguards.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Stakeholder Empathy & KPI Mapping","description":"Accurate incentive analysis and distinct non-contradictory audience framing.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Evidence & Ethical Balance","description":"Micro-story paired with credible metrics plus transparent downside acknowledgment.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Coalition Pre-Wiring & Objection Craft","description":"Constructive skepticism handling minus pushy coercion or reactance.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Adoption Design & Feasibility","description":"Low-friction workflow defaults, reversible pilot scope, and honest follow-up metrics.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('3f2731c7-1608-cad8-af4a-4b924d3a69d5', 'active-listening', 'active-listening-diagnostic-inquiry', '26309203-9ee8-2448-88a8-1ba6c7602e78'::uuid, 'Diagnostic Listening Transcript & Analysis Portfolio', 'Complete a practical active-listening challenge: conduct a 10–15 minute structured diagnostic or coaching conversation with a peer (or draft a realistic full verbatim client/team discovery dialogue + real reflection audit), clearly demonstrating (1) funnel questioning from broad to specific, (2) 3 natural content + emotion reflections, (3) comfortable silence holding, and (4) uncovered root insight vs. initial assumptions.', 'Highlight exact diagnostic questions, reflective labels, pause points, and closing "What else?" checks alongside honest self-critique on moments you felt urged to fix too early.', '["Annotated Dialogue Transcript or Recorded Audio/Video Notes (10–15 min session)","Breakdown of 3+ Natural Content & Emotion Reflections used","Before-vs-After Insight Log showing hidden constraints discovered via listening","Honest Self-Audit identifying 2 personal listening habits to sharpen next"]'::jsonb, 'Annotated transcript / PDF / DOCX / Audio or Video clip + reflection notes', 'Submit your annotated listening transcript or media recording plus your Before-vs-After insight reflection.', 25, 18, '["written","file","audio","video"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown","audio/mpeg","audio/mp4","video/mp4"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Open Diagnostic & Funnel Craft","description":"Clean neutral What/How questions progressing smoothly from broad to concrete.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Reflective & Emotion Precision","description":"Natural essence paraphrases and gentle emotion labels free of robotic scripts.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Restraint & Silence Discipline","description":"Zero premature fixing, balanced ~70% speaker exploration, effective pause holding.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Root Insight & Self-Audit Honesty","description":"Clear proof of uncovered real needs plus candid personal habit reflections.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('9a83ebfd-259f-9e78-a288-5706b8b375b9', 'conflict-resolution', 'workplace-conflict-resolution-mediation', '869bc319-eddd-ee92-5fed-312ef0a984e8'::uuid, 'Workplace Mediation & Behavioral Charter Case Pack', 'Step into the mediator role for an active escalation between Engineering and Client Success over rushed undocumented feature promises causing repeat weekend outages. Produce: (1) Root-Cause Conflict Diagnosis (task vs. process vs. relationship), (2) 30-Minute Mediation Script & Pivot Prompts, (3) 4-Rule Observable Behavioral Charter, and (4) 14-Day Follow-Up & Drift Repair Protocol.', 'Maintain strict multi-partial neutrality—do not favor either team—and ensure every charter rule passes the "can an outsider observe it objectively?" test.', '["Part 1: Conflict Root-Cause & Escalation Diagnosis","Part 2: 30-Minute Neutral Mediation Facilitation Script with I-statement & Pivot Lines","Part 3: 4-Rule Observable Behavioral Agreement Charter with exact SLAs","Part 4: 14-Day Check-In Agenda & Early Drift Correction Script"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written case pack or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four parts cleanly labelled showing balanced mediator neutrality.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Root-Cause Diagnosis Accuracy","description":"Clearly isolates systemic process/incentive gaps instead of stereotyping people.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Facilitator Neutrality & De-Escalation","description":"Balanced airtime, empathetic mirroring for both sides, and calm cooling pivots.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Observable Behavioral Charter Quality","description":"Actionable verifiable SLA rules replacing vague goodwill vows.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Follow-Through & Drift Repair Plan","description":"Practical 14-day review metrics and non-shaming early correction framing.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('aa53c59c-6554-33a0-2bab-1cab06e6e831', 'emotional-intelligence', 'emotional-intelligence-in-teams', '4af2c88f-6956-14a4-37d6-0e22873d7e37'::uuid, 'Personal EQ Charter & Real-Scenario Composure Audit', 'Construct a practical Personal Emotional Intelligence Operating Pack consisting of: (1) Your Personal Trigger & Choice-Gap Matrix (top 3 pressure triggers, bodily signs, reframing scripts), (2) Two Cognitive Distortion & Over-Functioning Empathy Audits, (3) A Clean Non-Hedged Relational Repair Script, and (4) A Team Psychological Safety Plan for high-stress weeks.', 'Ground every trigger, script, and boundary strictly in realistic workplace behaviors rather than abstract motivational slogans.', '["Part 1: Trigger Map, Bodily Cues & 60-Second Reset Choice-Gap Plan","Part 2: 2 Cognitive Reframing Drills + Sustainable Empathy Boundary Guidelines","Part 3: Non-Hedged Relational Repair & Group Voice Amplification Scripts","Part 4: High-Crunch Team Emotional Climate & Blind-Spot Calibration Plan"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written pack or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four parts cleanly labelled showing realistic workplace scenarios.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Self-Awareness & Regulation Depth","description":"Specific realistic triggers, bodily cues, and clean evidence-based cognitive reframes.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Sustainable Empathy & Boundaries","description":"Clear separation between caring support and unhealthy rescuing/burnout.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Relational Repair & Group Inclusion","description":"Non-hedged ownership language and practical voice-amplification actions.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Team Climate Integration","description":"Balanced high-standard + high-warmth system habits and realistic calibration cadence.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('9f5f03e6-2227-6403-f2a1-2a28a015ec39', 'leadership-and-teamwork', 'collaborative-leadership-teamwork', 'dae3abee-66d4-4942-e2fa-b35604807e0f'::uuid, 'Team Alignment Charter, Delegation & Turnaround Playbook', 'Assume the team-lead role for a struggling 5-person cross-functional launch pod experiencing dropped handoffs, micromanagement bottlenecks, loud-voice decision bias, and silent deadline slippage. Deliver a full turnaround playbook containing: (1) Shared Outcome Charter + 6-Row Clean RACI Matrix, (2) Structured Delegation Brief guarding against reverse delegation, (3) 20-Minute Silent-Pre-Write Decision & 35-Minute Blameless Retro Protocols, and (4) Caring Accountability Check-In Script.', 'Ensure every RACI row carries strictly one Accountable owner, retro limits commitments to 2 owned changes, and accountability script balances warm care with clear deadlines.', '["Part 1: Shared Launch Outcome Charter & Single-Accountable 6-Row RACI Table","Part 2: Guardrailed Delegation Brief & Reverse-Delegation Coaching Response","Part 3: Silent-Pre-Write Decision Protocol & 2-Action Blameless Retro Plan","Part 4: Private Missed-Commitment Accountability Script & Early-Risk Ritual"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written playbook or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four parts cleanly formatted verifying single Accountable RACI compliance.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Purpose Clarity & RACI Integrity","description":"Compelling shared outcome metric and crisp single-Accountable RACI lines.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Empowering Delegation Design","description":"Clear boundaries, authority tier, checkpoints, and coaching against reverse delegation.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Decision & Retro System Craft","description":"Anti-groupthink silent pre-write discipline plus realistic 2-action blameless retro.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Accountability Balance & Safety","description":"Caring yet firm private check-in language and blameless risk-flagging norms.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('1788ab7c-97da-97fb-cb4f-cd6d276c5c8a', 'critical-thinking', 'structured-critical-thinking-reasoning', 'f925cb3f-0bad-a4bd-5b30-30155ba21d8d'::uuid, 'Critical Reasoning Audit & Decision Stress-Test Pack', 'Evaluate a bold strategic proposal (e.g., launching an expensive unvalidated product line, copying a viral competitor playbook, or continuing a heavily sunk-cost 9-month internal tool) by producing a complete 4-part critical audit: (1) Argument & Hidden Assumption Map, (2) Bias, Fallacy & Causal Audit, (3) Steelman Case for the Opposing Strategy + Base-Rate Sanity Check, and (4) 20-Minute Pre-Mortem & Pre-Weighted 100% Decision Matrix.', 'Ensure hidden leaps, sample/confounder threats, strongest opposing rationale, and crisp guardrails appear transparently with balanced calibrated conclusions.', '["Part 1: Premise -> Unstated Assumption -> Conclusion Breakdown","Part 2: Cognitive Bias, Sunk-Cost, Fallacy & Correlation-vs-Causation Check","Part 3: Fair 200-Word Steelman Opposing Argument & Outside Base-Rate Test","Part 4: Pre-Mortem Failure Modes & Pre-Weighted Decision Criteria Matrix"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written audit or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four critical thinking sections clearly structured.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Assumption & Logic Deconstruction","description":"Accurately isolates silent leaps, premise strength, and causal vs. correlational pitfalls.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Bias & Fallacy Identification","description":"Sharp diagnosis of confirmation, survivorship, sunk-cost, or binary errors.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Steelmanning & Base-Rate Fairness","description":"Charitable high-integrity opposing case grounded in outside historical benchmarks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Pre-Mortem & Matrix Actionability","description":"Realistic preventable failure triggers plus balanced pre-locked weighted criteria.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('db5acee8-dbd0-0edf-ef0a-3b3a34d96474', 'problem-solving', 'root-cause-problem-solving', '4164cde9-a0b6-a426-68fb-43c39209ed63'::uuid, 'End-to-End A3 Root-Cause & Experiment Brief', 'Take one realistic recurring operational failure (e.g., 35% client onboarding delays, repeated billing invoice errors, high bug reopen rates, or stalled weekly reporting) and complete a rigorous A3 Root-Cause & Resolution Brief: (1) Non-prescriptive Measurable Problem Statement + MECE Issue Tree, (2) 5-Whys & Fishbone Systemic Diagnosis, (3) 6-Option Divergence + Impact-Effort Matrix, and (4) 7-Day Reversible Pilot Card with Guardrail Metric + Permanent SOP Hardening.', 'Verify every "Why" uncovers system/process mechanics rather than blaming operators lazily, and ensure pilot includes baseline metric, target metric, and clear quality guardrail.', '["Part 1: Baseline Problem Statement & 3-Branch MECE Decomposition","Part 2: Systemic 5-Whys Chain & Fishbone Cause Summary","Part 3: 6 Divergent Options & Weighted Impact-Effort Matrix","Part 4: 7-Day Pilot Experiment Card (Target + Guardrail + Second-Order Check + SOP Upgrade)"]'::jsonb, 'Structured A3 brief or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four parts cleanly labelled tracking clear root-to-fix traceability.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Problem Framing & MECE Decomposition","description":"Non-prescriptive measurable baseline and clean non-overlapping cause tree.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Systemic Root-Cause Depth","description":"Factual 5-Whys reaching process/validation roots rather than shallow blame.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Divergence & Triage Rigor","description":"Creative options including simplification/deletion plus clear Impact-Effort scoring.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Pilot Guardrails & Recurrence Lock","description":"Reversible experiment, balanced guardrail metric, ripple check, and permanent check update.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('938cc281-be5b-8ad5-531c-1ff27f0b00ac', 'presentation-skills', 'slide-visual-presentation-skills', 'c8ea9117-73f1-81fe-f8f5-6ba7e3d2d6a8'::uuid, '10-Slide Executive Deck Blueprint & Chart Makeover', 'Design a comprehensive 10-slide presentation architecture (plus 2 Q&A Appendix slides) for a realistic business recommendation, product pitch, or quarterly operational review. Provide: (1) Complete SCQA & 10-Action-Headline Horizontal Storyboard, (2) Full Visual Layout & De-Clutter Specification keeping live slides concise + high whitespace, (3) 2 Annotated Chart Makeover Specs fixing misleading/crowded defaults, and (4) Spoken Bridge Transitions, Midpoint Clock Anchor & Remote Engagement Plan.', 'Write actual exact action titles (no generic topic headings), specify layout grids/contrast accents, and keep live slide copy strictly concise.', '["Part 1: SCQA Outline & 10 Full-Sentence Action Headlines (+2 Appendix Headlines)","Part 2: Slide-by-Slide Visual Layout, Whitespace & Layout Type Specs","Part 3: 2 Decluttered Annotated Chart Designs (Type, Zero-Axis Rule, Accent Callout)","Part 4: Spoken Transition Cues, Remote Interaction Pulses & Time Buffer Plan"]'::jsonb, 'Structured deck blueprint or uploaded PDF/DOCX presentation + notes', 'Submit either an exported clean presentation PDF with presenter notes or structured blueprint document.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"SCQA & Action Headline Coherence","description":"Clear standalone story flow across all 10 headlines with crisp core Ask.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Visual Restraint & Layout Choice","description":"Sparse copy, high whitespace, clean hierarchy, and spatial grids beating bullet walls.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Honest Data & Chart Annotation","description":"Zero-axis integrity, muted contrast accents, and direct insight captions.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Delivery, Bridges & Time Control","description":"Natural slide-voice separation, crisp transitions, and solid Q&A/clock planning.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('f9caaf7d-34aa-8404-7263-cc686cf3eded', 'networking-and-relationship-building', 'authentic-networking-relationship-building', 'b9bb55fa-86bf-ba2f-79b2-f67bfa169f38'::uuid, 'Authentic Relationship-Building & Outreach Portfolio', 'Construct an actionable, ethical networking kit tailored to your target profession containing: (1) 8-Contact Dormant/Warm Tie Map + Value-First Hook for each, (2) 3 Crisp Respectful Outreach Messages (<100 words each: Dormant Reconnect, Cold Practitioner Note with Async Option, Closed-Advice-Loop Mentor Update), (3) 15-Minute Informational Coffee Chat Agenda & 4 High-Signal Questions + Graceful Branch Close, and (4) Double-Opt-In Intro Check + 30-Minute Weekly Maintenance Plan.', 'Ensure every outreach note cites specific believable context (zero "pick your brain" cliché), fits mobile viewing cleanly, and honors calendar boundaries.', '["Part 1: 8-Contact Dormant/Warm Tie Tracker & Thoughtful Value Ideas","Part 2: 3 Concise <100-Word Outreach & Advice-Loop Messages","Part 3: 15-Minute Informational Chat Script with Clock-Guard & Branching Close","Part 4: Double-Opt-In Intro Pair + Sustainable 30-Minute Friday Routine"]'::jsonb, 'Structured written portfolio or PDF/DOCX/Markdown upload', 'Submit all four parts cleanly formatted verifying concise <100-word outreach discipline.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","text/plain","text/markdown"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Outreach Specificity & Low Friction","description":"Brief <100-word messages showing real homework, zero \"pick your brain\", and easy reply paths.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Informational Inquiry & Time Respect","description":"Sharp craft questions, active clock guarding, and pressure-free branching closes.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Reciprocity & Double Opt-In Care","description":"Genuine value-first hooks, closed advice loops, and respectful intro verification.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Habit Sustainability & Authenticity","description":"Realistic 30-minute weekly maintenance cadence free of spammy gimmicks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('e25cd392-17a3-7555-a911-109024cd4f6e', 'general-writing', 'general-writing-foundations', 'ece2d6a0-ad80-8dba-5055-c4efb80cfb84'::uuid, 'Capstone: Publication-Ready 650-Word Explanatory Guide', 'Plan, draft, and systematically revise an original 600–750 word explanatory guide on a workplace, technical, or everyday craft topic of your choice.', '1. Submit a 1-sentence thesis + claim-driven outline.
2. Draft the full 600–750 word explainer featuring an engaging hook, informative subheadings, one concrete worked example, and a sharp synthesis closing.
3. Attach a brief revision note listing three concrete improvements made between your raw draft and final polished version (e.g., nominalizations fixed, macro trim, parallelism fix).', '"Final 600–750 word formatted explainer plus 1-paragraph outline and 3-item revision log."'::jsonb, 'Structured written submission or uploaded PDF/DOCX document.', 'Show clean before-and-after examples in your revision log so reviewers see your deliberate editing craft.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Sentence Clarity & Active Voice","description":"Strong subjects, concrete verbs, clean punctuation, minimal deadwood.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Structure, Topic Unity & Transitions","description":"Claim-led paragraphs with clear known-to-new progression and formatting.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Vocabulary Precision & Tone","description":"Measurable specifics replacing vague modifiers; consistent respectful register.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Documented Multi-Pass Revision","description":"Evidence of substantive macro and line improvements logged from raw draft.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('ca90e4e2-97dc-665a-4783-7240dfe77448', 'professional-writing', 'professional-writing-essentials', '002374b4-41a1-c398-cb11-8ed206140614'::uuid, 'Capstone: Decision Memo & Operational SOP Portfolio Packet', 'Prepare a complete two-part workplace writing portfolio: (1) a 1-page Decision Memo pitching an improvement to leadership with balanced options, and (2) an actionable 8-step SOP enabling a teammate to run part of that workflow independently.', 'Part A — Decision Memo (350–450 words): Include Summary Ask, Problem Impact, 3-Option Comparison (with clear recommendation), Risk/Mitigation, and Out-of-Scope boundaries.
Part B — Operational SOP: Include Metadata Freshness Header, Prerequisites, 8 numbered imperative steps with verification checkpoints, and a brief troubleshooting note.', '"Cohesive Decision Memo + Companion Operational SOP formatted cleanly in one PDF/DOCX or structured written response."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or neatly structured text submission.', 'Ensure names, metrics, and dates stay 100% consistent across both documents and clean of internal draft marks.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Bottom-Line Framing & Executive Readiness","description":"Recommendation, impact, cost, and deadline clear within top 10 lines.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Balanced Trade-Offs & Scope Boundaries","description":"Honest multi-option matrix plus realistic risk mitigations and exclusions.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"SOP Precision & Verification Flow","description":"Unambiguous prerequisites, single-action imperative steps, and checkpoints.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Tone, Formatting & Pre-Send Polish","description":"Scannable visual hierarchy, consistent vocabulary, and zero surface errors.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('7a93929b-dda7-6f6a-1efb-3dbd8ee7aa68', 'business-writing', 'business-writing-bluf-mastery', '8c1ab3a5-e384-4aab-dfdb-b623cdf75c22'::uuid, 'Capstone: Executive BLUF Business Case & 1-Page Scorecard', 'Write a 450–600 word executive BLUF business case recommending an operational, revenue, or cost-saving investment using the Pyramid Principle, MECE arguments, transparent financial assumptions, and red-team risk mitigations.', '1. Open with a 50-word BLUF summary (Recommendation, Impact, Cost, Ask Deadline).
2. Include a compact 4-cell Scorecard box.
3. Present 3 MECE supporting pillars backed by concrete assumptions and conservative downside break-even logic.
4. Close with 2 pre-answered CFO objections and an exact Next Steps owner block.', '"Polished 1–2 page executive BLUF business case + companion 90-word executive cover email."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or structured written memo.', 'Verify that every metric in your BLUF opener matches your scorecard and analytical pillars seamlessly.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"BLUF Clarity & Executive Opening","description":"Conclusion, quantified stakes, and exact ask crystal clear inside first 50 words.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Pyramid Logic & MECE Grouping","description":"Distinct, non-overlapping pillars clearly proving the governing thesis.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Financial Honesty & Risk Red-Teaming","description":"Transparent unit logic, conservative break-even bounds, and thoughtful mitigations.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Reconciliation, Cover Email & Layout","description":"100% consistent metrics, sharp action headings, and effortless 90-second scan.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('c7326ba4-2b9c-8618-dacb-0ff74adf073f', 'creative-writing', 'creative-writing-foundations', 'e8daafd7-04a1-f5e3-8f70-1bf6c6844a4f'::uuid, 'Capstone: Original 700–900 Word Complete Short Scene & Revision Audit', 'Write an original self-contained short narrative (700–900 words) anchored in single Limited POV showing clear protagonist desire, subtext dialogue, a decisive scene turn, and a deliberate filter-word revision trim.', '1. Submit a short 3-line story blueprint (POV, Active Want, Turn).
2. Deliver a 700–900 word narrative featuring grounded sensory setting, 10+ lines of subtext-rich dialogue, and zero head-hopping.
3. Append a brief Revision Note detailing 3 concrete edits made (filter words removed, slow opening trimmed, or action beat replacing an adverb).', '"Blueprint + polished 700–900 word short story/scene + 3-point revision note."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly formatted written text.', 'Check every dialogue line aloud and strip hidden filter verbs ("saw", "felt", "realized") in your final polish.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Sensory Immediacy & POV Discipline","description":"Vivid physical grounding, minimal filter distance, strictly consistent POV.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Desire, Tension & Scene Turn","description":"Clear protagonist goal meeting credible resistance and genuine status shift.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Subtext Dialogue & Voice","description":"Natural indirect tension paired with crisp invisible tags/action beats.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Pacing Control & Revision Craft","description":"Tight opening, varied rhythm, and concrete evidence of structural/line cuts.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('784fc3e0-18ee-51bf-87e3-c343f35ea3e0', 'storytelling', 'storytelling-narrative-craft', '53b0fa40-d41a-310e-59bb-066a8d4dbc2b'::uuid, 'Capstone: Accordion Applied Narrative Package (600-Word + 60-Second Spine)', 'Craft a true or realistic applied workplace, community, or personal breakthrough story rendered in two synchronized versions: a complete 550–700 word narrative article AND a tight 60-second spoken accordion script backed by one ethical/delivery audit.', '1. Submit the full 550–700 word narrative built on "But/Therefore" causality, grounded single-person stakes, one zoomed turning snapshot, and blended human-scale metrics.
2. Provide the compressed 60-word/60-second Accordion Script preserving complication + insight.
3. Add 3 concise notes marking [PAUSE] delivery beats, slide visual idea, and consent/credit attribution.', '"Accordion 2-format narrative package + delivery/ethics cues."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written submission.', 'Check every paragraph for passive "and then" chaining—make tension force every turn naturally.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Causal Spine & Human Stakes","description":"Clear \"but/therefore\" causality anchored in concrete single-subject tension.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Zoom Snapshot & Blended Proof","description":"Memorable turning-point detail paired gracefully with human-scaled evidence.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Accordion Compression Integrity","description":"60-second version preserves core friction, turn, and meaning completely.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Ethical Framing, Delivery & Closing","description":"Dignified credit, non-preachy reflection, and practical pause/visual cues.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('db8f4ae0-37c8-7ca8-933c-71d8979995a2', 'copywriting', 'copywriting-conversion-craft', '26c7c179-eeee-6b63-f7a7-75855638222c'::uuid, 'Capstone: Full Conversion Landing Page Blueprint & Microcopy Suite', 'Write a complete, ethical conversion landing page copy deck (550–750 words) for a real or realistic digital tool, service, or educational program anchored in VoC outcomes, a continuous subhead spine, PAS/AIDA flow, specific proof, and hypothesis-led A/B test plans.', '1. Specify Target Buyer & Core Rule-of-One Promise.
2. Write Hero Section (Headline, Objection-Clearing Subhead, Value-Led CTA + Risk Reversal).
3. Build Scannable Body using clear benefit H2s: Problem/PAS hook, How It Works, Specific Before/After Proof Placeholder, 3 Objection-Clearing FAQs.
4. Propose 2 structured VoC-backed A/B test hypotheses for Hero or CTA.', '"Full landing page copy deck + microcopy & CTA labels + 2 structured A/B hypotheses."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written deck.', 'Verify that reading ONLY your Hero H1 and section H2 lines tells the complete persuasive story cleanly.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Outcome Clarity & Hero Value Prop","description":"Crisp 5-second clarity grounded in tangible buyer gains over empty buzzwords.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Subhead Spine & PAS/AIDA Flow","description":"Logical scroll architecture linking empathy, mechanism, proof, and CTA smoothly.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Objection Defenses, Proof & Microcopy","description":"Specific before/after proof structure, transparent FAQs, and zero-hype CTAs.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Ethical Framing & A/B Hypotheses","description":"Zero dark patterns paired with actionable, insight-backed conversion test plans.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('42dd5ebb-f7ca-c9f2-5cb9-80c7a259514c', 'technical-writing', 'technical-writing-documentation', '28535f22-56ee-6c60-4239-326b33bdb121'::uuid, 'Capstone: Diataxis Micro-Doc Pack (How-To + API Reference + Release Note)', 'Create a cohesive 3-piece documentation package for a realistic software feature or API tool demonstrating Diataxis separation, runnable validity, tabular clarity, and release-note communication.', '1. Part A (How-To Guide): 7–9 numbered location-first imperative steps with upfront Prerequisites, expected terminal/UI check output, and 2 exact Troubleshooting pairs.
2. Part B (API Reference Entry): Standardized endpoint spec (`POST /v1/...`) listing Method, Auth, typed Parameter Table (with realistic constraints/enums), strict valid copyable `curl` + JSON 201 response (zero comments inside JSON!), and a 4xx error response.
3. Part C (Release Note): Clean categorized changelog entry highlighting 1 Breaking Migration Notice clearly.', '"Complete 3-part developer documentation pack cleanly formatted in Markdown/PDF/text."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX/MD or structured written submission.', 'Verify every JSON payload parses strictly cleanly and ensure UI/API term names match 100% across all three docs.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Diataxis Discipline & Procedural Precision","description":"Zero intent mixing; location-first imperative steps with clear prerequisites.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"API Schema Rigor & Valid Examples","description":"Explicit parameter types/enums, realistic values, strictly parseable JSON payloads.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Tables, Output Checks & Troubleshooting","description":"Expected confirmations, searchable exact error patterns, and structured comparison tables.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Style Polish & Actionable Changelog","description":"Clean simple present tense, consistent terms, and crystal-clear breaking migration notice.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('5bd2c1f7-fb31-5507-9e27-ad5cf894c60e', 'academic-writing', 'academic-writing-evidence-synthesis', 'e05032de-3c37-dd43-4dfb-07701e9b506c'::uuid, 'Capstone: 850-Word Academic Literature Synthesis & Annotated Reverse Outline', 'Write a focused 800–950 word analytical literature synthesis mini-paper centered on an arguable research thesis, integrating at least 4 cited sources (real or clearly referenced course/academic frameworks) via thematic dialogue, MEAL structure, calibrated hedging, and transparent limitation analysis.', '1. Provide a funnel Introduction leading to a clear contestable Thesis.
2. Write 3 MEAL-structured Synthesis body paragraphs comparing concepts/perspectives thematically (zero serial author-by-author summaries and zero dropped quotes).
3. Include one Steelmanned Counterargument + honest Scope Limitation block.
4. Attach consistent Reference List (APA or consistent style) + brief paragraph-by-paragraph Reverse Outline proving thesis alignment.', '"800–950 word scholarly synthesis + formatted References + Reverse Outline check."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written paper.', 'Verify none of your paragraphs close abruptly on a raw parenthetical citation—always end with your own synthesis/link.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Thesis Focus & Funnel Gap Framing","description":"Narrow contestable claim anchored cleanly in scholarly tension and scope.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Thematic Source Synthesis & Integrity","description":"Active dialogue among sources, smooth paraphrase, zero dropped quotes.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"MEAL Paragraph Rigor & Hedging","description":"Substantive analysis per evidence piece paired with calibrated non-overclaimed certainty.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Counterargument, Limits & Citation Parity","description":"Fair objection engagement, honest bounds, exact in-text/reference 1:1 parity.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('ccc3eb91-2fee-0ec5-496e-50d113724f49', 'report-writing', 'report-writing-analytical-briefs', '56197295-683d-620f-b59f-17b58cfd8026'::uuid, 'Capstone: Complete Analytical Operational Audit & Feasibility Brief', 'Produce an end-to-end 700–900 word structured analytical report evaluating a realistic workplace bottleneck, audit finding, or vendor feasibility choice complete with Executive Summary, Scope/Methods, Impartial Numbered Findings, Traceable Recommendations, and Distribution Handoff Note.', '1. Executive Summary (~120 words): No-new-data synthesis of Scope, Top Findings, and Priority Recommendations.
2. Scope & Methodology Box (Period, exact Sample `n`, Exclusions).
3. Numbered Findings (`F1`, `F2`, `F3`) strictly neutral, paired with at least one aligned Comparison Table and raw `n` metrics.
4. Traceable Recommendations (`R1`, `R2`, `R3`) mapping directly back to `F` IDs with Effort/Priority/Suggested Owner + brief Pre-Send Handoff Email.', '"Structured 700–900 word analytical report + formatted table + 80-word review handoff email."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly formatted written report.', 'Verify zero blame adjectives live inside Findings and reconcile every single Executive Summary number against body figures.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Modular Structure & Executive Synthesis","description":"Self-contained page-one brief aligned 100% with verified body sections.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Methodology, Denominators & Visual Table","description":"Clear timeframe/exclusions, `n` counts paired with metrics, clean aligned tables.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Strict Findings-vs-Recommendations Split","description":"Impartial factual Findings separated cleanly from traceable owner-mapped Recommendations.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Precision, Rounding Parity & Handoff","description":"Consistent formats/decimals, calm neutral tone, and decision-led pre-read note.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('588d71bf-ccba-d9c9-9f25-8d90bb40bf70', 'email-writing', 'email-writing-workplace-outcomes', '1d255743-fdfb-ae3f-64c0-b82dd035d833'::uuid, 'Capstone: 4-Scenario High-Trust Workplace Email Portfolio', 'Write a cohesive portfolio of four realistic workplace/client emails showcasing flawless subject design, 3-block scannability, diplomatic boundaries, crisp `To/CC/BCC` framing, and zero pre-send slips.', '1. Email 1 (Action Decision): `[Decision Needed...]` request presenting 2 clean options with zero-friction close.
2. Email 2 (Diplomatic Boundary/De-escalation): Politely declining an extra out-of-scope rush task OR calmly recovering an erroneous delivery.
3. Email 3 (Personalized Cold Outreach): <100-word authentic networking/mentor/client pitch with specific hook + micro-ask.
4. Email 4 (Clean Forward Summary): Condensing a noisy internal chain into a 3-bullet `TL;DR` brief + explicit `To`/`CC` assignments.', '"4 complete emails formatted with Subject, To/CC headers, body text, and clean plain signature."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written text.', 'Verify every email keeps paragraphs 1–3 lines tall, asks clearly on its own line, and includes accurate time-zone/date tags.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Subject Triage & Mobile Hierarchy","description":"Action-frontloaded subjects paired with airy 1–3 line blocks and isolated asks.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Boundary Grace & De-Escalation","description":"Firm kindness, accountable ownership, zero passive-aggressive clichés.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Cold Specificity & Forward Synthesis","description":"Tight sub-100-word personalization and concise multi-reply TL;DR abstraction.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Header Discipline & Signature Hygiene","description":"Accurate `To/CC` roles, clean time zones, lightweight plain signatures.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('77bc02ee-5f15-15cb-6fff-5250c99bafb6', 'blogging', 'blogging-editorial-publishing', '1b9b7f14-7614-d1aa-02bc-e19432560032'::uuid, 'Capstone: 900-Word Cornerstone Blog Article & Distribution Kit', 'Write an original, publication-ready 850–1,000 word educational or teardown blog article anchored in one clear pillar, complete with an APP hook, scannable H2s/buckets, one concrete worked example, contextual content-upgrade CTA, and multi-channel native distribution drafts.', '1. Declare Target Reader Persona & Editorial Pillar.
2. Deliver a polished 850–1,000 word article featuring 3 headline options, <95-word APP opener, descriptive H2 spine, one realistic worked example/comparison, descriptive inline links, and focused ending question + contextual opt-in CTA.
3. Attach one 130-word native social takeaway post promoting the guide without spam.', '"Complete cornerstone blog article + 3 headlines + contextual opt-in + 130-word native promo draft."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX/MD or cleanly formatted written article.', 'Check mobile paragraph rhythm (max 3–4 lines) and ensure zero thin generic bullet padding exists.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Reader Fit, Headline & APP Hook","description":"Sharp audience focus, compelling specific titles, crisp <95-word APP opener.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Scannable Flow & Original Depth","description":"Descriptive subheads, conversational bridges, rich concrete worked examples.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Closing Synthesis & Relevant CTA","description":"Actionable focused ending prompt paired smoothly with aligned opt-in offer.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Native Distribution & Voice Polish","description":"Value-first standalone social adaptation plus consistent authentic voice.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('1c5d71d0-a496-d1f8-4ee0-999d8d2f30a9', 'scriptwriting', 'scriptwriting-audio-video', 'ba256488-c291-2e1c-a51e-d91d81622500'::uuid, 'Capstone: Two-Column 90-Second Explainer Script & Vertical Reel Cut', 'Produce a complete production-ready script packet containing: (1) a 90-second (~195-word) Two-Column Audio/Visual instructional or explainer script complete with cold open, visual counterpoint, `[BEAT]` marks, and forward loop; plus (2) a tightly cut 35-second (~75-word) vertical short-form adaptation.', '1. Header Metadata: Target Audience, Format, Target Runtime, Exact Spoken Word Count (~135 WPM check).
2. Part A (90s A/V Table): Clean Left Column (`Time | Visual / Screen Text / B-Roll`) alongside Right Column (`Spoken VO / [BEAT] / Phonetic Notes`) using crisp conversational contractions and zero robotic slide-reading.
3. Part B (35s Vertical Short Cut): Zero-greeting Frame-1 visual text + punchy <80-word spoken adaptation + silent-play caption check.
4. Table-Read Note: 2 concrete trims made after reading aloud.', '"Locked production metadata + 90s A/V two-column script + 35s vertical cut + 2 table-read refinements."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly formatted written script table.', 'Time both spoken columns aloud against a real stopwatch before submitting—ensure spoken lines sound effortless.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Ear-Readiness & Word Timing Accuracy","description":"Natural spoken rhythm hitting realistic ~130–145 WPM breath budgets cleanly.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Two-Column A/V Complementary Design","description":"Sharp [VISUAL] counterpoint cues adding depth instead of narrating screen text verbatim.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Cold Open Hook & Vertical Cut Compression","description":"Zero-latency 5-second value confirmation plus tight silent-friendly 35s adaptation.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Markup Polish & Table-Read Edits","description":"Clean `[BEAT]` chunking, production metadata headers, and logged aloud cuts.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('5c1fbb3a-cd79-5790-e573-e37eac7c2b16', 'content-strategy', 'content-strategy-editorial-systems', 'f19a43a0-4750-5890-7968-7517d2bc8bf7'::uuid, 'Capstone: 90-Day Strategic Content Architecture & Governance Playbook', 'Design a comprehensive, ready-to-execute Content Strategy Playbook (700–900 words) for a real or realistic digital product, educational platform, or service business—uniting ROT Audit findings, a Pillar-Cluster map, a 1-page writer Content Brief, SME/Atomization cadence, and intent-matched KPIs.', '1. Business & Audience North Star: Define core mission bottleneck and buyer/learner persona.
2. Mini ROT Audit Plan: Show 4 realistic existing/legacy asset decisions (`Keep`, `Refresh`, `Merge`, `Prune`).
3. Pillar-Cluster Hub: Map 1 strategic Pillar Hub + 5 connected Cluster Spokes balanced across funnel intent.
4. Full Production Content Brief for Spoke #1 (including explicit Differentiator Angle + 3 SME interview prompts).
5. Atomization Matrix (1-to-4 derivative plan) + Intent-Matched Quarterly Scorecard including 1 qualitative/dark-social check.', '"Complete 90-day strategic playbook cleanly formatted with tables/lists."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written strategic document.', 'Verify funnel metrics match exact article stages (never score an onboarding help doc solely by raw cold traffic!).', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Strategic Alignment & ROT Audit Logic","description":"Crisp tie to business friction plus disciplined Keep/Update/Merge/Prune decisions.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Pillar-Cluster & Funnel Balance","description":"Cohesive bi-directional hub structure blending buyer-intent depth cleanly.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Actionable Brief & SME/Atomization Engine","description":"Clear 1-page brief specification, pragmatic SME Q&As, native channel adaptations.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Measurement Realism & Governance Clarity","description":"Intent-matched KPIs, dark-social tracking, and clean accessible standards.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('76fae52e-27b7-1ecf-0211-ae7fff81f2b2', 'editing-and-proofreading', 'editing-proofreading-standards', 'f7ade902-0491-6d93-005a-8131f0619e93'::uuid, 'Capstone: Multi-Pass Editorial Transformation, Style Sheet & Author Queries', 'Demonstrate complete mastery across all four editing lenses by evaluating, polishing, normalizing, and querying a realistic rough ~350-word multi-defect article excerpt (self-selected or provided sample scenario below) into publication-grade form.', '1. Select or write a realistic "Rough Draft Excerpt" (~250–320 words) containing explicit realistic bugs (at least 1 macro gap, dangling modifier, pleonasm, hyphen error, UK/US or number inconsistency, weekday-date mismatch or math contradiction, and subtle confusable typo).
2. Supply a clean **Polished Final Copy** preserving warm author voice while resolving every flaw.
3. Deliver an **8-Rule Style Sheet**, **Fact/Math Correction Note**, and **3 Constructive `[AQ]` Author Queries** + **Editor Delivery Cover Note**.', '"Rough annotated vs. clean final copy + 8-rule Style Sheet + Fact/Math Notes + 3 AQs."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured text showcase.', 'Clearly label your Rough Draft defects separately so reviewers evaluate your surgical precision cleanly!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Line Compression & Syntactic Accuracy","description":"Dangling modifiers, parallelism, tautologies, and hyphens resolved cleanly without flattening voice.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Style Sheet & Uniform Copyediting","description":"Consistent dialect, casing, dashes, numeric style, and clean sequence parity.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Fact, Math & Confusable Verification","description":"Sharp detection of numeric/percentage-point traps, dates, and spellcheck-safe confusables.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Constructive Author Queries & Polish","description":"Helpful collaborative AQs paired with clean visual proof gate standards.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('2a0e431b-0a8f-e4f9-c876-658b0f28ce3a', 'seo-writing', 'seo-writing-search-intent', '2c1d78df-d437-e1ab-edc3-ea33bb21e12f'::uuid, 'Capstone: Search-Intent Brief, E-E-A-T Article Blueprint & On-Page Optimization Spec', 'Produce an end-to-end ethical SEO Writing & On-Page Architecture deliverable (750–900 words) targeting one realistic user query: combining Intent Analysis, Complete Metadata Spec, an E-E-A-T-rich snippet-ready Guide Excerpt (~450 words), and Internal Linking/Refresh Governance.', '1. Intent & Query Brief: Target Query, Intent Classification, Competitor Depth Gap identified.
2. Snippet & Metadata Spec: Evergreen URL Slug, `<title>` (<58 chars verified), Meta Description (<150 chars verified), and strict `H1 -> H2 -> H3` outline.
3. Live Draft Section (~450 words): Include ONE question-style `H2` followed immediately by a sharp 45-word direct answer block, genuine firsthand proof/caveat signals (`E-E-A-T`), and natural fluent prose with zero stuffing.
4. Internal Link & Cannibalization Note: Specify 2 descriptive inbound/outbound internal link targets plus one Linkable Asset / Striking-Distance refresh metric plan.', '"Full SEO Brief + verified metadata + 450-word snippet-ready E-E-A-T body excerpt + linking spec."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured Markdown/text deck.', 'Verify exact character counts on Title and Meta Description and confirm every `H2/H3` flows smoothly with zero repeated keyword awkwardness.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Search Intent Match & Metadata Limits","description":"Accurate intent diagnosis, evergreen URL, strict <58-char title & <150-char meta.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Semantic H1-H3 & Answer-First Snippets","description":"Clean semantic hierarchy paired with crisp 40–55 word direct answer blocks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"E-E-A-T Depth & Zero-Stuffing Fluency","description":"Concrete lived evidence/caveats written smoothly for humans without spam repetition.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Internal Links, Anti-Cannibalization & Refresh","description":"Descriptive anchor flows, `site:` check logic, and practical refresh/asset plan.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('a6fd24c7-bd76-29ca-48c2-0ea0f575f040', 'entrepreneurship', 'entrepreneurship-foundations', '0a6a29e1-4b16-e3d3-47cd-a6f98fed0a8a'::uuid, 'Capstone: Lean Venture Validation Dossier & 90-Day Launch Blueprint', 'Construct a complete, reality-grounded Lean Venture Plan (750–950 words) launching an ethical small product or service—spanning Beachhead Pain Analysis, Mom-Test Question Script, Concierge MVP Experiment Design, Realistic Unit Economics Math, First-10 Stranger Acquisition Plan, and Day-1 Operational Hygiene.', '1. Beachhead & Workaround Pain: Define your narrow segment + current messy alternative.
2. Mom-Test Discovery Script: List 4 strict past-behavior discovery questions (zero "would you pay?" traps).
3. 7-Day Concierge Experiment: Exact manual delivery test + clear quantitative Pass/Fail metric threshold.
4. Unit Economics & Break-Even Math: Price, honest Variable Cost breakdown, Contribution Margin, Fixed Overhead, exact Break-Even monthly units.
5. First-10 Outreach + Operational Safeguards: Specific non-friend acquisition plan, written scope/deposit rule, and 60-day Pivot/Scale review criteria.', '"Structured 750–950 word venture validation dossier + unit-math breakdown."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly formatted written dossier.', 'Double-check unit contribution math (`Price - Variable > 0`) and ensure every Mom-Test prompt examines past actions rather than future predictions.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Pain Urgency & Unbiased Mom-Test Design","description":"Verified costly workarounds paired with 4 behavioral past-tense discovery prompts.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Concierge MVP & Beachhead Positioning","description":"Scrappy 7-day manual test with pre-set clear quantitative pass/fail gates.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Unit Economics & Cash Flow Accuracy","description":"Correct contribution margin, realistic variable deductions, exact break-even math.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Stranger Acquisition, Hygiene & Pivot Rigor","description":"Practical First-10 path, clean deposit/bank separation, disciplined review gates.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('c8130351-470a-eaae-c46f-1474808d8cf2', 'business-development', 'business-development-partnerships', 'c01ad0a5-d88a-c21b-55cb-baa4e17609be'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End Strategic Partnership Proposal, Term Sheet & Enablement Kit', 'Architect a realistic, launch-ready Business Development Partnership Package (750–950 words) uniting Partner Selection Thesis, Mutual Value Pitch Email, Crawl-Walk-Run Pilot Plan, 1-Page Term Sheet, Frontline Rep Cheat Sheet, and Channel Conflict Policy.', '1. Target Partner Profile & Ecosystem Rationale: Pick a real or realistic non-competing complementary organization and pinpoint the exact partner retention/gap KPI your alliance strengthens.
2. Tailored Outreach Pitch (<120 words) + Crawl Pilot Design: Propose ONE concrete Tier-1 Co-Marketing/Referral pilot with measurable 60-day Gate Criteria (zero premature exclusivity).
3. 1-Page Attribution & SLA Term Sheet: Registration mechanics, 90-day lookback cutoff, net-cash payout trigger, 24-hr SLA, and clean 30-day exit clause.
4. Rep Cheat Sheet & Conflict Guardrail: Exact 2 trigger phrases, 15-second copy-paste intro snippet, plus explicit internal sales commission neutrality policy.', '"Full strategic partnership dossier + 1-page term sheet + frontline enablement card."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written playbook.', 'Ensure mutual benefits address the partner’s strategic metric upfront rather than reading like a greedy one-sided vendor pitch.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Strategic Ecosystem Fit & Mutual Upside","description":"Clear alignment solving partner’s core retention/gap bottleneck fairly.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Crawl-Walk-Run Pilot & Verifiable Gates","description":"Smart low-friction starting test paired with unambiguous happy-ears-proof milestones.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Attribution Fairness & SLA Governance","description":"Clear pipeline lookback, cash-collected payouts, 24-hr intro SLAs, graceful exit.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Rep Enablement & Channel Neutrality","description":"Practical 15-sec intro card plus zero-conflict internal commission alignment.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('acc68ed7-112d-eed4-eb36-be6ecabcd4f0', 'business-planning', 'business-planning-operating-models', '6da62af6-f984-e21f-b76e-bf925d91eff3'::uuid, 'Capstone: Living 12-Month Operating Model, Driver Math & Risk Playbook', 'Construct a cohesive, crisp living Business Operating Plan (750–950 words) for a real or realistic business—uniting Annual Focus & Deferred Trade-Offs, Bottom-Up Driver & Capacity Modeling, Quarterly OKRs, a Weighted Risk Matrix with Pre-Committed Scenario C Cash Triggers, and a 90-Day Rolling Cadence.', '1. Core Operating Identity & Deferred Scope: 3 top annual strategic priorities PLUS 2 explicitly deferred bright ideas (protecting capacity).
2. Bottom-Up Revenue & Capacity Equation: Show literal driver steps (`Leads/Visitors -> Close Rate -> Avg Value -> Max Fulfillment Hours/Staffing Trigger at 85%`)—zero top-down "% of billion market" guesses.
3. Q1 OKR & Weekly Scorecard: 1 focused Objective, 3 outcome Key Results (zero activity traps!), 5 weekly leading metrics + single-owner labels.
4. Risk Matrix & Scenario C Trigger: Top 3 specific concentration/operational vulnerabilities + literal numeric Downside Brake rule.
5. Rolling 90-Day Reset Plan + Pre-Mortem note explaining one hidden crash scenario prevented upfront.', '"Complete structured living business plan dossier + capacity/driver math + risk/OKR tables."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly formatted written operational playbook.', 'Check that your bottom-up weekly outreach/traffic volume realistically reconciles against your stated monthly staff fulfillment hours!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Strategic Focus & Explicit Exclusions","description":"Sharp prioritization balanced cleanly with realistic parked scope guardrails.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Bottom-Up Drivers & Capacity Triggers","description":"Verifiable operational arithmetic tying funnel inputs neatly to 85% capacity gates.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Outcome OKRs & Weekly Pulse Design","description":"Measurable impact Key Results, quality guardrails, leading scorecard, single owners.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Risk Realism, Pre-Mortem & Cash Brakes","description":"Concentration checks, explicit numeric Scenario C triggers, crisp rolling loop.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('ab5a5f3f-0473-22b9-06fe-e51ee38c25b7', 'startup-fundamentals', 'startup-fundamentals-mvp-traction', '5a6d5bea-69d6-f3af-4222-4f587fb4b397'::uuid, 'Capstone: Lean Startup Validation Spec, MVP Blueprint & Traction Playbook', 'Create an actionable, zero-fluff Startup Validation & Launch Playbook (750–950 words) for a fresh startup concept—moving rigorously from Leap-of-Faith Risk Ranking and 72-Hour Wizard-of-Oz MVP Scope straight through Falsifiable Test Rules, OMTM/Retention Diagnostics, Monthly Mentor Digest, and Four-Lights Scale Gates.', '1. Concept & Riskiest Assumptions: One-sentence target persona + top 3 Leap-of-Faith beliefs ranked cleanly.
2. Core Loop & Wizard-of-Oz MVP: Define the 3-step Core "Aha!" Loop + exact features brutally CUT from v1 + behind-the-curtain manual shortcuts.
3. Pre-Committed Test Hypothesis: Write 1 falsifiable experiment statement with literal numeric Minimum Success Criterion + costly user action.
4. Metrics & Runway Hygiene: Declare Stage OMTM, define healthy Cohort Flattening check, calculate sample Net Burn / Runway example.
5. Rolling Launch + Sample Monthly Update: 3-step iterative release loop + sharp 80-word sample Monthly Stakeholder Digest featuring one exact 2-minute Ask.', '"Structured startup blueprint + cut-list MVP spec + test hypothesis + sample stakeholder digest."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written startup plan.', 'Ensure your MVP experiment requires meaningful real action (deposit, live onboarding data, or calendar lock)—not passive "liked landing page" clicks.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Risk Ranking & Falsifiable Hypothesis","description":"Sharp leap-of-faith focus paired with pre-set costly numeric pass/fail gates.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Wizard-of-Oz MVP & Core Loop Restraint","description":"Clean minimal 3-step aha flow plus fearless documented v1 feature cuts.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Cohort/OMTM Rigor & Runway Math","description":"Accurate separation of retention/OMTM from vanity stats plus realistic net-burn calculation.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Rolling Launch, Candor & Scale Gates","description":"Practical non-stealth testing loop, crisp update w/ Ask, Four-Lights checks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('8dd1ec2b-63bc-ea62-2833-216a93e497da', 'business-model-development', 'business-model-development-economics', '29be0f0b-85bf-107a-8540-ec5b511ce5da'::uuid, 'Capstone: Full Business Model Architecture, Unit Math & Sensitivity Dossier', 'Architect a comprehensive, financially grounded Business Model Blueprint (750–950 words) covering a coherent 9-Block Canvas Alignment, Value Metric & Revenue Engine Rationale, Fully Calculated Margin-Adjusted LTV / Loaded CAC / Payback Period, Competitive Moat Design, and a 3-Shock Sensitivity Stress Test.', '1. Cohesive 9-Block Summary & Value Metric: Define buyer segment, channel mechanics, clean 3-tier pricing structure, and why your Value Metric aligns fairly with growth.
2. Exact Quantitative Unit Economics Walk-Through: Supply explicit Price, COGS/Delivery %, Gross Margin $, Monthly Churn %, Loaded CAC (including labor/tools!), computed Gross-Margin LTV, LTV:CAC Ratio, and CAC Payback Months.
3. Margin & Moat Engine: Explain one Productized/Modular cost shield plus one Earned Switching-Cost Moat (zero dark lock-ins!).
4. 3-Shock Stress Matrix: Recompute Payback/Viability under +40% CAC surge and +2% monthly churn hike—specifying exact protective model upgrade (e.g., annual pre-pay or onboarding tier).', '"Structured business model playbook + worked arithmetic proof + 3-shock stress matrix."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly formatted written dossier.', 'Verify Gross Margin % is explicitly multiplied into your LTV numerator and Monthly Gross Profit Payback denominator!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Canvas Coherence & Value Metric Alignment","description":"Seamless fit between buyer price, sales channel effort, and fair scaling metric.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Unit Economics Arithmetic Rigor","description":"Exact verified Gross-Margin LTV, Loaded CAC, LTV:CAC, and Payback months calculations.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Cost Leverage & Earned Moat Integrity","description":"Practical modularization/variable protection paired with non-hostage loyalty moats.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Quantitative Stress-Test & Evolution","description":"Accurate recalculation under shocks plus smart defensive model adjustments.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('ca9caa5e-9868-fa40-1cdc-eea92b331eb0', 'market-research', 'market-research-customer-validation', '7b51bb81-4538-e5d1-a51b-f965c2fdc3d3'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End Market Validation Study, Unbiased Survey & JTBD Brief', 'Design and execute a complete, realistic Market Research & Customer Validation Dossier (750–950 words) testing a clear business hypothesis—spanning Mixed-Method Qual/Quant Architecture, 5 Unbiased Survey Items, JTBD Switching Force Matrix, Bottom-Up TAM/SAM/SOM Math, 3-Competitor White-Space Scan, and a Behavioral Persona Decision Card.', '1. Research Hypothesis & Qual Guide: Define decision uncertainty + 4 non-leading past-behavior discovery prompts.
2. Unbiased Survey Pack: Draft 5 crisp atomic survey items covering balanced scales, clean non-overlapping brackets, N/A opt-outs, and zero double-barreled flaws.
3. JTBD & Switching Matrix: Map Push, Pull, Anxiety, and Habit forces + specify 1 anxiety-lowering solution fix.
4. Bottom-Up TAM/SAM/SOM: Calculate bottom-up figures transparently citing plausible real buyer universe counts x realistic annual price.
5. Competitor Gap + Behavioral Persona: 3-competitor review gap check + 1 zero-fluff Behavioral Persona Card driving 2 concrete strategic decisions.', '"Complete validation dossier + 5-item survey + bottom-up sizing math + behavioral persona."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written validation report.', 'Verify every survey prompt asks strictly ONE clear unbiased dimension and verify bottom-up SAM math shows explicit multiplication!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Qual-First Design & Unbiased Survey Mechanics","description":"Behavioral interview prompts + crisp atomic neutral survey items with clean brackets.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"JTBD Switching Forces & Empathy Depth","description":"Sharp Push/Pull/Anxiety/Habit diagnosis pairing triggers with real anxiety remedies.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Credible Bottom-Up TAM/SAM/SOM Sizing","description":"Transparent verified count x realistic unit pricing calculations free of 1% fantasy.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Competitor White Space & Behavioral Synthesis","description":"Fair incumbent review analysis + zero-fluff Persona card driving crisp team action.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('0f915e51-6209-ebc8-608f-5726a9e88aab', 'financial-literacy', 'financial-literacy-cashflow-margins', 'd7e5ffa8-027d-2d6c-7671-f0a21d801a06'::uuid, 'Capstone: Managerial Financial Literacy & Decision Readiness Diagnostic', 'Analyze and produce a complete, crystal-clear Financial Health & Decision Brief (750–950 words) integrating exact Margin-vs-Markup Pricing Math, Break-Even Analysis, a 6-Week Cash Trough Forecast identifying timing risks, Working Capital Upgrades, and a Loaded Hiring Readiness Verdict.', '1. Pricing & Break-Even Repair: Take a sample `$45` direct-cost item currently sold at `+35% markup` (`$60.75`); calculate its ACTUAL Gross Margin %, calculate exact price needed for true `45% Gross Margin`, and determine monthly Break-Even units covering `$5,500` fixed overhead.
2. Cash Timing & 6-Week Trough Check: Show why `+12k P&L Profit` can accompany empty checking via a realistic 6-week cash snapshot table (`Opening Cash, Expected Cleared Collections, Payroll/Tax/Vendor Outflows`) pinpointing the lowest cash week.
3. Working Capital & Controls: Recommend 2 specific collection/deposit levers + 2 basic anti-fraud/tax controls (`Callback rule, Tax Vault, Segregation`).
4. Loaded Hiring Verdict: Test whether a `$4,000` base salary (`1.25x loaded = $5,000/mo`) hire is safe right now by stating exact extra monthly revenue needed at your repaired `45% Gross Margin` plus 90-day ramp reserve.', '"Complete financial diagnostic brief with verified step-by-step arithmetic & weekly timing table."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written financial brief.', 'Double-check every division (`$45 / (1 - 0.45) = $81.82` and `$5,000 / 0.45 = $11,111.11` extra sales)—precision builds instant financial trust!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Margin vs Markup & Break-Even Accuracy","description":"Flawless repair from markup trap to true target margin price and exact break-even volume.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Cash Timing & Weekly Trough Identification","description":"Clear 6-week literal cash trace catching mid-period timing dips missed by monthly P&L.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Working Capital & Dual Financial Controls","description":"Pragmatic deposit/billing shifts paired cleanly with BEC callback, tax vault, and dual checks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Loaded Hiring Math & Executive Clarity","description":"Accurate 1.25x loaded payroll + required sales break-even calculation cleanly justified.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('ef335d6b-00a9-fecf-1a99-a880b9146dea', 'small-business-management', 'small-business-management-operations', '1d0e3eba-9e93-5882-51bd-f7c9b3d725e0'::uuid, 'Capstone: Practical Small-Business Operations & Systemization Playbook', 'Build a complete, ready-to-deploy Small Business Operations Manual Blueprint (750–950 words) transforming a chaotic founder-dependent shop, studio, or agency into a calm systemized team operation across SOP Checklists, ABC Inventory/Vendor Resilience, Hiring/Coaching, LAST Service Recovery, and Weekly Focus Cadence.', '1. Daily Bottleneck Checklist SOP + Visual Shift Handoff Rule: Pick 1 error-prone workflow and write a crisp 8-box actionable checklist + central shift handoff protocol.
2. ABC Stock & Backup Supply Rule: Show 1 worked Reorder Point math example + active Backup Vendor verification cadence.
3. Team Work-Sample & 4-Step Coaching Plan: Design a 15-min realistic hiring work-sample check + concise Tell-Show-Do-Check outline.
4. Empowered LAST Recovery Guide: Define clear frontline dollar allowance + exact 4-step LAST recovery response script for 1 realistic glitch.
5. Owner Focus Calendar & Peak-Surge Guardrails: Weekly `"Working ON"` protection rule + 3 peak-season resilience safeguards (`cutoffs, menu trim, 2FA`).', '"Structured operations manual packet + math checks + scripts + resilience checklists."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured operational playbook.', 'Keep every checklist step crisp and behavioral—imagine a busy Week-1 hire scanning it standing at a counter in 45 seconds!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Checklist SOP & Shift Handoff Clarity","description":"Actionable fast-read SOP avoiding owner bottlenecks plus shared exception tracking.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Inventory Math & Vendor Resilience","description":"Accurate Reorder Point calculation + active-tested backup vendor design.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Work-Sample Hiring & Hands-On Coaching","description":"Realistic job simulation check paired smoothly with Tell-Show-Do-Check training.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"LAST Recovery, Owner Focus & Peak Prep","description":"Autonomous recovery empowerment, Working-ON protection, clean seasonal/2FA rules.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('de6fa981-92c6-a7da-5ec4-14e1c29cb9c4', 'sales-fundamentals', 'sales-fundamentals-consultative-closing', '08e1bf5e-a0f4-88da-a809-5a1abb72f259'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End Consultative Discovery, Objection & Closing Playbook', 'Construct a cohesive, high-trust Consultative Sales Playbook (750–950 words) for a realistic B2B service, software tool, or coaching program—covering an Upfront Contract & Layered Discovery Guide, a Buyer-Centric Mutual Action Plan, a 3-Tier Proposal Opener, Calm Objection Scripts, and Sales-to-Delivery Handoff.', '1. Call #1 Upfront Contract & Diagnostic Script: Write a natural 60-sec opening contract + 4 layered Situation -> Pain -> Quantified Impact -> Compelling Event prompts (zero interrogative tone!).
2. Tailored 15-Min Demo Outline + Reverse MAP: Map a concise `Tell-Show-Verify` flow plus a 5-step reverse Mutual Action Plan working back from an exact buyer Launch Date.
3. Value-Anchored 3-Tier Proposal Summary: Mirror quantified pain stakes above 3 crisp tiered scope choices (`Core / Recommended Full / VIP`).
4. Calm Objection Responses: Write non-defensive Empathize-Clarify-Isolate answers for `"Too expensive"` AND `"Too swamped to switch right now"`.
5. Handoff & Habit Guardrail: 5-field Sales-to-Delivery Handoff Brief + steady anti-feast/famine prospecting block.', '"Complete consultative sales playbook + discovery prompts + MAP + objection scripts + handoff brief."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written sales playbook.', 'Verify none of your objection scripts argue defensively or give naked discounts without adjusting scope or isolating true blockers first!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Upfront Contract & Layered Impact Discovery","description":"Warm safe opening paired with deep cost-of-inaction impact questions.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Tailored Demo, Reverse MAP & Tiered Framing","description":"Pain-focused Tell-Show-Verify, shared MAP timeline, smart 3-tier options.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Calm Diagnostic Objection Resolution","description":"Zero defensiveness or blind discounting; genuine isolate-and-resolve poise.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Closing Ask, Handoff Brief & Prospecting Rhythm","description":"Low-pressure clear close, detailed delivery handoff, sustainable daily habit.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('8525c96c-69fc-e148-1dd6-015a1839b505', 'customer-relationship-management', 'customer-relationship-management-retention', '26caa592-4854-65d4-6cdf-50bb064fcc7a'::uuid, 'Capstone: Full-Lifecycle CRM Architecture, Health Score & Retention Playbook', 'Architect a lean, pragmatic Customer Relationship & Retention Operating Playbook (750–950 words) tailored to a recurring business or multi-client agency—spanning a Minimalist CRM Schema, First-72-Hour Behavior-Triggered Onboarding, 4-Signal Health Scoring + Save Play, Outcome QBR Agenda, and Privacy/Tiered Care Governance.', '1. Minimalist CRM Schema & Suppression: Define 4 lean CRM objects with strictly <=6 core fields each + explicit Next-Date and Open-Ticket Suppression rules.
2. TTFV Onboarding Plan: Pinpoint exact 72-hr First-Value Win + 2 behavior-triggered branch responses (Fast Mover vs. Day-7 Stalled).
3. Health Matrix & Yellow Save Script: Detail 4 crisp Health signals (including Champion Departure!) + calm 90-word 60-day pre-renewal rescue outreach.
4. Outcome QBR & Ethical Expansion Trigger: Concise 25-min client-centered QBR outline + Green-Health expansion check.
5. Privacy & Tiered Care Grid: 4 strict CRM privacy rules (objective notes, export lock, 2FA, opt-out) + sustainable Tech-vs-High touch split.', '"Structured CRM & retention playbook + schemas + scripts + privacy governance."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written operational playbook.', 'Verify every automated prompt explicitly honors active urgent-ticket suppression and fast-mover skip branches!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Minimalist Schema & Suppression Logic","description":"Uncluttered practical objects, required Next-Dates, clear ticket suppression.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"TTFV Speed & Behavioral Branching","description":"Concrete 72-hr first win paired cleanly with stalled-user rescue logic.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Health Rigor, Champion Risk & Rescues","description":"Balanced 4-signal scorecard spotting quiet churn and sponsor exits early.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Outcome QBR, NRR Ethics & Data Care","description":"ROI-first QBR outline, Green-gated upsells, strict objective privacy controls.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('ab80fa1f-7d40-abda-0896-68139267a0c2', 'branding', 'branding-positioning-identity', '73f5dacf-0227-b35b-d93c-ce53ba81fc82'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End Brand Positioning, Voice & Distinctiveness Charter', 'Create an authoritative, fluff-free Strategic Brand Charter (750–950 words) transforming a real or realistic business into an unmistakable market brand—uniting April Dunford Positioning Architecture, Observable Brand Promise, Paired Voice Polarities + Outage Tone Flex, Category-Contrast Distinctive Assets, Branded House Expansion Logic, and Commercial Lift Metrics.', '1. Dunford 5-Step Positioning Map: Competitive Alternatives (`including manual status quo`), Unique Capabilities, Quantified Value, Best-Fit Target, Chosen Market Category Frame.
2. Observable Promise & Proof: One testable non-cliché Brand Promise + 3 concrete operational Proof Pillars (verify zero "world-class/innovative" fluff!).
3. Voice Polarity Charter: 3 `"We Are X, Never Y"` pairs + 2 concrete Copy Swaps + 1 Crisis/Outage Tone Shift rule.
4. Category-Contrast Distinctive Assets & Branded House Plan: Identify 2 competitor visual/verbal clichés to invert purposefully + specify 2 new sub-offers cleanly named under Branded House logic (passing Radio Test!).
5. Brand Health Scorecard: 3 non-vanity commercial signals tracking brand lift over 12 months.', '"Complete 5-part strategic brand charter + copy examples + naming architecture."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written brand playbook.', 'Apply the Logo-Cover Test directly onto your central Promise—make sure top rivals could NOT swap their name over yours effortlessly!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Dunford Positioning & Category Fit","description":"Sharp alignment from realistic alternatives to unique concrete value and category framing.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Observable Promise & Paired Voice Guardrails","description":"Non-fluff verifiable core promise backed by clear \"This/Not That\" and outage tone flex.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Distinctive Contrast & Branded House","description":"Smart inversion of rival clichés + cohesive radio-test-safe unified sub-offer naming.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Living Adoption & Brand Lift Metrics","description":"Practical lightweight kit habits + measurable commercial brand health signals.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('c8870bb9-f69f-57a5-9a94-471ec43d2e56', 'product-management', 'product-management-specs-launches', '85785ab7-8e44-b41d-9b73-e154f86ccaeb'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End Lean PRD, Opportunity Map & Ethical Launch Blueprint', 'Produce an authoritative Product Management Package (750–950 words) framing one realistic software or digital product initiative—spanning Outcome/Opportunity Framing (with 3 candidate solutions), Transparent RICE Trade-off rationale, Complete 1-Page Lean PRD (`happy/empty/error/permission` states + Non-Goals), Telemetry & Counter-Metric Guardrails, Tiered Support Launch Plan, and Humane Ethical Check.', '1. Opportunity & Ideation Triad: Define measurable Target Outcome + validated User Opportunity + 3 distinct solution paths showing why your chosen slim fix wins cleanly over bloated Idea #1.
2. Prioritization & Tech Capacity Note: Show transparent RICE scoring comparison against 1 competing shiny distractor + brief 15% tech-health note.
3. Crisp Lean PRD: Problem/Evidence, Success + 2 Guardrail Metrics, Core Workflow, 4 concrete Edge States (`Empty, Loading, Error, Permission`), and 3 explicit Out-of-Scope Non-Goals.
4. Telemetry + Staged Rollout: Exact 3 tracked event names + Canary Rollout (`Internal -> 10% -> 100%`) + Day-14 audit plan.
5. Tiered GTM & Ethical Guarantee: Support 48-hr briefing steps + confirm zero dark patterns inside UX/defaults.', '"Structured product strategy dossier + Lean PRD + telemetry & launch readiness spec."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written PRD package.', 'Verify all four UI edge states (`Empty, Loading, Error, Permission`) sit explicitly inside your PRD acceptance table alongside Non-Goals!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Outcome Focus & Multi-Solution Discovery","description":"Clear root goal, genuine pain diagnosis, 3 contrasting candidate solutions cleanly compared.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Lean PRD Clarity, Edges & Non-Goals","description":"Concise problem framing, explicit 4 edge states, strict protective Non-Goals.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Telemetry, Counter-Metrics & Rollout","description":"Exact Day-1 events, balancing quality guardrails, safe canary launch & audit.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Support Readiness, Roadmap & Ethics","description":"48-hr ahead frontline briefing, Now-Next-Later honesty, smart defaults without dark patterns.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('26141c82-8473-24eb-7385-6639f71cacd4', 'project-management', 'project-management-delivery', 'f92b2e75-1933-74b6-89b1-cc9cde9fb260'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End 6-Week Project Charter, WBS, RAID & Launch Playbook', 'Plan a realistic 6-week cross-functional delivery project end-to-end (750–950 words)—delivering a tight 1-Page Project Charter with Non-Goals, a <=3-Day Work Breakdown & Critical Path, an actionable Top-5 RAID Register, a realistic Weekly RAG Stakeholder Brief + Scope Change Trade-off script, and a safe Staged Launch & Retrospective Closure Plan.', '1. Project Charter & Non-Goals: Crisp goal, deliverables, single DRI owner, fixed deadline, and explicit Out-of-Scope exclusions + Change-Control script.
2. WBS & Critical Path: 3 deliverables decomposed into 12+ concrete tasks (`<=3d`), flagging external calendar waits and the Critical Path.
3. Active RAID Log: 5 genuine specific threats/assumptions paired with Early Triggers and Preventive actions.
4. Weekly RAG Update & Escalation: Realistic <=200-word Amber update presenting concrete Option A/B sponsor decision.
5. Safe Go-Live & Closure: 8-point Launch/Rollback plan + Operational Handoff + 2 blameless system-level retro tweaks.', '"Full-lifecycle project planning playbook (`Charter, WBS, RAID, RAG, Launch & Closure`)."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written delivery package.', 'Double-check every WBS task represents concrete verifiable completion (`<=3 days`) with an explicit single owner!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Charter Clarity & Non-Goals Rigor","description":"Crisp Done state, explicit phase exclusions, and realistic trade-off framing.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Granular WBS & Critical Path Realism","description":"Logical <=3-day breakdown separating active effort from real wait queues.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Preventive RAID & Constructive RAG Brief","description":"Actionable early-tested assumptions paired with crisp <=200-word Amber escalation.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Safe Staged Rollout & Blameless Closure","description":"Reversible rollout sequence, operational handoff, and concrete system tweaks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('c9aa0f7e-5793-668e-3eb1-aa68dfd397e1', 'strategic-thinking', 'strategic-thinking-decision-making', 'd010c4ac-669c-32bd-eccc-e558393db172'::uuid, 'Capstone: Comprehensive Strategy Kernel, Moat Wedge & Quarterly Bet Playbook', 'Craft a sharp executive Strategy Playbook (750–950 words) for a real or realistic business/team—replacing vague goal slogans with a complete Strategy Kernel (`Diagnosis, Guiding Policy + Explicit Trade-Offs, Coherent Actions`), a Durable Moat & Counter-Positioning Wedge analysis, a 1st/2nd-Order Consequence & Pre-Mortem review, and a crisp 2-Bet Quarterly Execution + Kill-Trigger Sheet.', '1. Strategy Kernel & Explicit Refusals: Honest root Diagnosis + Guiding Policy naming 3 clear items you deliberately say NO to + 3 mutually reinforcing Actions.
2. Moat & Asymmetric Wedge: Diagnose real structural defensibility vs. copyable fluff + define 1 Counter-Positioning wedge slow giants avoid.
3. Consequence Trace & Pre-Mortem: Map 2nd-order ripples of your top choice + run a crisp 4-point Pre-Mortem with concrete early mitigations.
4. Quarterly 2-Bet Execution & Commander’s Intent: Strictly 2 Quarterly Bets (`Leading + Guardrail + Day-60 Kill Criterion`) + 2 sharp `"X Even Over Y"` frontline decision rules.', '"Executive Strategy Kernel, Moat, Pre-Mortem, and Execution Playbook."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written strategic brief.', 'Check strictly that your Guiding Policy carries genuine visible cost/trade-offs—if zero tempting revenue was declined, sharpen it!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Strategy Kernel & Real Trade-Offs","description":"Sharp root diagnosis, coherent actions, and honest uncomfortable strategic refusals.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Moat Depth & Asymmetric Counter-Positioning","description":"Realistic structural barrier focus and smart non-imitable niche wedge.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"2nd-Order Thinking & Candid Pre-Mortem","description":"Anticipated incentive ripples and candid failure causes tied cleanly to fixes.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Quarterly Discipline & Commander’s Intent","description":"Balanced Leading/Guardrail bets, honest Kill criteria, sharp Even-Over rules.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('e767a7b9-e75c-f1ee-37e8-2bb00008b82b', 'business-negotiation', 'business-negotiation-dealmaking', '44819a55-e24c-0727-1ce1-82301ddf7034'::uuid, 'Capstone: Comprehensive Deal Prep, MESO Strategy, Objection Scripts & Safeguard Playbook', 'Prepare a thorough end-to-end Negotiation Playbook (750–950 words) for a high-stakes client retainer, B2B vendor contract, or career partnership—encompassing concrete BATNA/ZOPA math, a 3-bundle profitable MESO menu, verbatim Tactical Empathy (`Label + Calibrated How`) counter-scripts for 3 hardball tactics, a 5-point Written Deal Recap, and balanced Contract Safeguards.', '1. Deal Prep & BATNA Sheet: Detail Target, Walk-Away Floor, concrete verified BATNA, counterparty interests, and Principled Opening Anchor.
2. Profitable 3-Option MESO Menu: 3 genuinely distinct bundles trading non-price terms (`timing, scope, upfront split, case rights`) maintaining equal fair margin.
3. Hardball & Objection Scripts: Verbatim Mirror + Label + Calibrated `How/What` replies for Price Pushback, Late Nibble, and Gracious Walk-Away.
4. Written Deal Recap & Fair Safeguards: Same-day 5-bullet confirmation recap + 4 balanced protections (`deposit, acceptance window, delivery-tied balance, kill/pause rule`).', '"Full-cycle negotiation brief, MESO menu, spoken scripts, recap, and contract safeguards."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded PDF/DOCX or cleanly structured written deal playbook.', 'Verify all 3 MESO options genuinely deliver equal healthy margin—and never concede anything without a paired Get!', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"BATNA Discipline & Principled Anchor","description":"Concrete fallback plan, crisp walk-away floor, and objective market-anchored opening.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Diagnostic 3-Bundle MESO Design","description":"Genuine asymmetric variable trades yielding balanced healthy economics across all three.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Tactical Empathy & Counter-Scripts","description":"Poised zero-defensive Labels, calibrated How/What framing, and dignified Walk-Away.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Written Recap & Mutual Safeguards","description":"Crystal same-day 5-bullet recap plus fair symmetric payment and scope protections.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('dcd1754c-c54c-3d85-8e62-f4be67eb8139', 'social-media-management', 'social-media-community-growth', '965709ff-e1ed-ad00-39bc-deeaeaec1ce7'::uuid, 'Capstone: 30-Day Social, Page & Community Growth Blueprint', 'Design a practical 30-day organic social, Facebook Page governance, and community engagement plan for a real or realistic brand or your own niche personal brand.', '1. Define target audience, 1-line positioning/Bio, and 4 balanced content pillars.
2. Outline a 2-week (6-post) sample calendar specifying Pillar, Native Format, Hook line, and CTA.
3. Document Facebook Page setup hygiene (CTA button, Admin/2FA rule, 2 Saved Replies) + 4 concise Community Charter rules.
4. Specify 3 success metrics (beyond raw followers) and 1 owned-audience opt-in bridge.', '"Structured multi-section organic social & community plan (written brief or PDF/DOCX document)."'::jsonb, 'Written strategic plan or uploaded PDF/DOCX brief.', 'Write realistic word-for-word hooks and saved replies rather than generic placeholders like "Post something educational Monday".', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Positioning & Balanced Pillar System","description":"Clear audience clarity and disciplined mix across educate, proof, community, and offer pillars.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Sample Calendar & Native Hook Quality","description":"Scroll-stopping, phone-friendly hooks and specific CTAs across multi-format posts.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Page Hygiene, Moderation & Saved Replies","description":"Concrete 2FA/admin governance, personalized reply templates, and fair community rules.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Insights & Owned-Channel Bridge","description":"Meaningful KPIs (saves, replies, UTM clicks) paired with ethical newsletter/resource capture.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('b0fd29f9-9d49-77da-7baf-a736c339547d', 'facebook-and-instagram-advertising', 'paid-social-meta-ads-mastery', '83df0ef3-f548-d6e8-7c9d-9b816b8819ce'::uuid, 'Capstone: Full-Funnel Meta Ads Campaign Blueprint & Diagnostic Pack', 'Architect an end-to-end Facebook & Instagram paid campaign blueprint for a realistic product or service—covering account structure, signal hygiene, 6-variant creative test matrix, and diagnostic rules.', '1. Define Objective, Target Funnel Event, Break-Even CPA math, and clean 2-Campaign Consolidation structure (Winners + Creative Sandbox) with buyer exclusions.
2. Document tracking hygiene (Standard Events + Browser/CAPI deduplication via `event_id` + UTM schema).
3. Write 3 distinct buyer Angles x 2 hooks each (compliant with Meta policy, zero personal-attribute violations) + 1 warm objection-busting retargeting concept.
4. Define your Hook Rate / CTR / Frequency scaling & fatigue rules.', '"Complete Meta Ads Campaign Blueprint (structured text brief or PDF/DOCX/CSV upload)."'::jsonb, 'Structured written brief or uploaded PDF/DOCX document.', 'Write realistic compliant ad headlines/primary text and explicit budget math rather than generic checklists.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Account Structure & Objective Alignment","description":"Clean conversion objective, budget consolidation avoiding fragmentation, and accurate buyer exclusions.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Signal Integrity & Attribution Hygiene","description":"Clear Pixel + CAPI deduplication logic, UTM structure, and blended MER awareness.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Creative Test Matrix & Policy Compliance","description":"Distinct angles with scroll-stopping compliant hooks across native 4:5/9:16 formats.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Diagnostic & Scaling Discipline","description":"Clear Hook/Hold/CTR troubleshooting logic and disciplined stepped scaling rules.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('55e90439-6dcb-dda3-b66a-8cef0ede988c', 'google-ads', 'search-marketing-google-ads-sem', 'cd1f6768-635e-7851-b64c-24b3fc10363d'::uuid, 'Capstone: Integrated SEO + Google Ads Search Capture Plan', 'Design a coordinated Search Engine Marketing (SEO + Google Ads) blueprint for a real or realistic business capturing high-intent search buyers cleanly.', '1. Map 10 search keywords cleanly across Informational (SEO guides) vs. Transactional (Service/Product landing + Google Ads) with 8+ Negative Keywords.
2. Write an optimized On-Page SEO specification (Title Tag <60 chars, Meta Description <155 chars, clean URL slug, H1 + 3 H2s, and 2 internal link plans).
3. Build one tightly themed Google Ads Search Ad Group (6 Exact/Phrase keywords, 6 distinct RSA headlines, 2 descriptions, 4 Sitelinks, strict Geo Presence rule).
4. Define Primary vs. Secondary conversion rules plus Blended Search CAC metric.', '"Structured Search Marketing Plan (written brief or PDF/DOCX/CSV upload)."'::jsonb, 'Structured written submission or uploaded PDF/DOCX document.', 'Check character bounds (~50–60 chars Title) and ensure every RSA headline stays crisp and distinct.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Search Intent & Keyword/Negative Architecture","description":"Clear separation of Informational vs. Transactional queries plus smart pre-launch negatives.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"On-Page & Technical SEO Precision","description":"Sharp Title/Meta, semantic H1–H2 outline, crawl/canonical hygiene, and contextual internal links.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Google Ads Ad Group & Quality Score Fit","description":"Tight theme, diverse modular RSA copy, relevant Sitelinks, and safe location/network controls.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Signal Integrity & Blended SEM Strategy","description":"Clean Primary vs. Secondary rules, Brand vs. Non-Brand isolation, and paid-to-SEO feedback loop.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('51c84adb-a5e4-4147-a352-2219f4a543c6', 'email-marketing', 'email-content-lead-generation', 'efadf170-766a-5f5b-ce32-902d8433218c'::uuid, 'Capstone: Integrated Lead Gen, Email, Content & Creator Launch Pack', 'Build a cohesive owned-audience acquisition package linking one targeted Lead Magnet, a 4-email Lifecycle Welcome Sequence, 2 supporting Content/Creator pieces, and deliverability/segmentation guardrails.', '1. Define target buyer persona + high-intent Lead Magnet (with headline, 3-field max capture spec, and why it filters non-buyers).
2. Draft a full 4-email Welcome & Nurture Sequence (Day 0, 2, 4, 6) with sharp Subject + Preview lines, one CTA each, and Behavioral Segmentation rule.
3. Outline 1 BOFU/MOFU Content asset + 1 Micro-Creator Partnership Brief (vetting criteria, `#ad` rule, UTM + code tracking, usage rights).
4. Include your Deliverability Checklist (SPF/DKIM/DMARC, bounce/spam limits, 120-day sunset rule).', '"Full Owned Growth Blueprint (structured text or PDF/DOCX submission)."'::jsonb, 'Structured written submission or uploaded PDF/DOCX document.', 'Write realistic subject lines, preview lines, and email bodies cleanly—avoid vague notes like "Email 2: tell a story".', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Lead Magnet & Capture Fit","description":"Actionable, high-intent opt-in resource with friction-appropriate capture spec.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Welcome Sequence & Lifecycle Copy","description":"Distinct 4-email arc with sharp Subject/Preview hooks, single CTAs, and clean segmentation.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Content Funnel & Creator Brief","description":"Information-gain content piece paired with fair, policy-safe, tracked creator partnership plan.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Deliverability & Governance Hygiene","description":"Sound SPF/DKIM/DMARC, consent clarity, sunset policy, and action-focused metrics.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('70ca0a59-9054-77f7-e17a-afc374aa0c7d', 'marketing-analytics', 'marketing-analytics-cro-strategy', '45ac87df-da64-cc7e-dc73-aa9856f377d6'::uuid, 'Capstone: End-to-End Analytics, CRO & Growth Strategy Audit', 'Produce an executive-grade Analytics, CRO, and Marketing Strategy Audit for a realistic growth business—linking clean measurement, margin math, empirical experimentation, and strategic channel focus.', '1. Define a standardized UTM Taxonomy table (5 channels) + reconciliation rule handling cross-platform attribution overlap (MER + post-purchase prompt).
2. Present a worked Unit Economics check (Price, Gross Margin %, Churn/Repeat, Max Allowable CAC, Payback window) + diagnose one mock funnel leak.
3. Draft 2 evidence-backed CRO Experiment Cards (Because/If/Then hypothesis, Primary Metric, Guardrail Metric, full-week duration/SRM check).
4. Write a crisp 1-page Marketing Strategy framing ICP Wedge, 70-20-10 Channel Allocation, and explicit "Not Doing This Quarter" trade-offs.', '"Comprehensive Analytics, CRO & Growth Strategy Pack (structured text brief or PDF/DOCX/CSV upload)."'::jsonb, 'Structured written submission or uploaded PDF/DOCX document.', 'Show exact worked math (`LTV`, `CAC`, `MER`) and concrete CRO hypotheses grounded in observed user friction.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"UTM Hygiene & Attribution Rigor","description":"Strict lowercase taxonomy, zero internal UTMs, and sound blended MER reconciliation.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Unit Economics & Funnel Bottleneck Math","description":"Margin-adjusted LTV, realistic CAC/payback ceilings, and surgical leak diagnosis.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"CRO Research & Experiment Discipline","description":"Evidence-led hypotheses paired with sound statistical duration, SRM, and guardrail checks.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Strategic Positioning & Resource Focus","description":"Sharp ICP wedge, smart channel-model fit, 70-20-10 allocation, and explicit trade-offs.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('dc37627c-4725-cbdb-99fe-0210d42b8150', 'ui-ux-design', 'ui-ux-digital-product-design', '627d3a93-99b4-0074-d8b5-a3bb91b84062'::uuid, 'Capstone: Accessible UI/UX Flow, Diagram & Responsive Spec Pack', 'Take one realistic messy digital workflow (e.g., clinic booking, freelance invoice portal, or event signup), ideate divergently, visualize the flow, design an accessible responsive UI spec, and outline a usability test plan.', '1. Summarize Problem & Constraints + show 3 contrasting divergent concept options (and why #1/finalist won).
2. Diagram the complete User Flow including Ideal, Empty, Loading, and Error recovery states.
3. Specify an accessible component & responsive layout plan (8px spatial scale, >=4.5:1 contrast, visible labels, >=44px mobile touch targets, desktop-to-375px mobile card/table reflow, semantic tokens).
4. Write 3 unbiased usability task prompts + Severity 1/2/3 ranking criteria.', '"Full UI/UX Design & Visual Systems Pack (structured written brief or PDF/PNG/Figma link)."'::jsonb, 'Structured written brief, uploaded PDF/PNG mockups, or public prototype URL.', 'Show exact color contrast/token specs and write zero-hint usability prompts free of UI button names.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Creative Ideation & Constraint Framing","description":"Sharp problem constraints and genuinely contrasting divergent concepts evaluated objectively.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Visual Flow & Edge-State Completeness","description":"Clear non-cluttered process flow covering Ideal, Empty, Loading, and Error states cleanly.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Accessibility & Responsive Craft","description":"Sound 8px grid, >=4.5:1 contrast, persistent form labels, focus/touch rules, and 375px reflow.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Usability Test & Handoff Rigor","description":"Unbiased goal-based test tasks, clear severity triage, and tokenized design-to-dev clarity.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('34f69552-fef0-0987-6281-9cd34cafb58a', 'brand-identity-design', 'canva-and-brand-identity-design', 'c32a0fc9-43b6-1b5d-66c0-153cdbd27b09'::uuid, 'Capstone: Cohesive Brand Identity, Canva Kit & Art Direction System', 'Develop a complete Brand Identity, Canva Production Template Spec, and Art Direction Manual for a realistic business ready for consistent real-world execution.', '1. Define Brand Positioning, 3 Visual Polarities, and Logo Suite specs (Horizontal, Stacked, 24px Submark + clear-space + 3 monochrome/Do-Don’t rules).
2. Specify 60-30-10 Color System (HEX + CMYK awareness + explicit WCAG AA text contrast matrix) and 2-Font Typographic Scale.
3. Write an Art Direction Brief (lighting mood, color temperature, authentic props, copy-safe negative space rules).
4. Detail 3 Canva Master Templates (4:5 Carousel Cover with 1:1 safe-crop zone, Inner Slide, Flyer) noting locked layers and defensive text anchoring + clean client Handoff Folder tree.', '"Full Brand Kit & Art Direction Pack (PDF/PNG visuals or comprehensive structured design spec)."'::jsonb, 'Uploaded visual Brand Deck (PDF/PNG), public Canva link + written rationale, or structured brief.', 'Verify actual contrast numbers across your text/background color pairs and define concrete 1080x1350 margin pixel guides.', 25, 18, '["written","file","project_url","screenshot"]'::jsonb, '["application/pdf","image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","text/plain","text/markdown","text/csv"]'::jsonb, 25, true, '[{"id":"r1","label":"Strategic Fit & Scalable Logo Suite","description":"Clear differentiation from clichés plus coherent Horizontal/Stacked/Submark and clear-space rules.","maxPoints":7,"weightPercent":28},{"id":"r2","label":"Palette Contrast & Typographic Hierarchy","description":"Disciplined 60-30-10 palette with verified AA text pairs and modular 2-font scale.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r3","label":"Canva System & Defensive Template Spec","description":"Smart margin discipline, center-safe 4:5 framing, layer locking, and non-fragile text anchoring.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24},{"id":"r4","label":"Art Direction & Production Handoff","description":"Cohesive shoot/photo rules, copy-safe scrim framing, and clean RGB/CMYK licensed asset tree.","maxPoints":6,"weightPercent":24}]'::jsonb),
    ('6228e93a-0f60-8bfc-c568-68781ca73a23', 'video-editing', 'photography-video-motion-production', '1dbc9191-4efa-7520-1b0d-ad0da431c121'::uuid, 'Capstone: Integrated Photo, Video & Motion Short Production Pack', 'Plan and execute (or produce complete production blueprints & sample artifacts for) a cohesive visual story combining directional-light photography, 45–60s video pacing/audio spec, and eased motion captioning.', '1. Document a 5-Shot Visual Storyboard (Hook Detail, Medium Subject, Wide Context, POV, Payoff) with exact natural lighting & background cleanup rules.
